1
00:00:31,334 --> 00:00:34,326
GALADRIEL [IN SINDARIN]:
<font color="#00bd00"><i>I amar prestar aen.</i></font>

2
00:00:34,535 --> 00:00:36,401
[IN WESTRON] <i>The
world is changed.</i>

3
00:00:36,425 --> 00:00:37,764
<font color="#00bd00"><i>Han mathon ne nen.</i></font>

4
00:00:37,788 --> 00:00:39,859
<i>I feel it in the water.</i>

5
00:00:39,883 --> 00:00:41,518
<font color="#00bd00"><i>Han mathon ne chae.</i></font>

6
00:00:41,542 --> 00:00:43,711
<i>I feel it in the earth.</i>

7
00:00:43,735 --> 00:00:46,021
<font color="#00bd00"><i>A han noston ned 'wilith.</i></font>

8
00:00:46,046 --> 00:00:49,049
<i>I smell it in the air.</i>

9
00:00:49,466 --> 00:00:51,343
<i>Much that once was...</i>

10
00:00:51,552 --> 00:00:53,136
<i>...is lost.</i>

11
00:00:53,804 --> 00:00:56,848
<i>For none now live who remember it.</i>

12
00:01:09,778 --> 00:01:14,157
<i>It began with the forging
of the Great Rings.</i>

13
00:01:14,408 --> 00:01:16,326
<i>Three were given to the Elves:</i>

14
00:01:16,493 --> 00:01:20,289
<i>Immortal, wisest and fairest
of all beings.</i>

15
00:01:21,331 --> 00:01:23,417
<i>Seven to the Dwarf-lords:</i>

16
00:01:24,167 --> 00:01:28,589
<i>Great miners and craftsmen
of the mountain halls.</i>

17
00:01:29,047 --> 00:01:30,299
<i>And nine...</i>

18
00:01:30,507 --> 00:01:33,510
<i>...nine rings were gifted
to the race of Men...</i>

19
00:01:33,719 --> 00:01:37,556
<i>...who, above all else, desire power.</i>

20
00:01:39,224 --> 00:01:43,895
<i>For within these rings was bound
the strength and will to govern each race.</i>

21
00:01:45,397 --> 00:01:48,567
<i>But they were all of them deceived.</i>

22
00:01:48,817 --> 00:01:50,902
<i>For another ring was made.</i>

23
00:01:52,279 --> 00:01:55,324
<i>In the land of Mordor,
in the fires of Mount Doom...</i>

24
00:01:55,741 --> 00:02:00,203
<i>...the Dark Lord Sauron forged
in secret a Master Ring...</i>

25
00:02:00,412 --> 00:02:02,456
<i>...to control all others.</i>

26
00:02:02,664 --> 00:02:06,627
<i>And into this Ring he poured
his cruelty, his malice...</i>

27
00:02:06,835 --> 00:02:11,048
<i>...and his will to dominate all life.</i>

28
00:02:12,007 --> 00:02:15,886
<i>One Ring to rule them all.</i>

29
00:02:16,720 --> 00:02:18,388
<i>One by one...</i>

30
00:02:18,597 --> 00:02:23,268
<i>...the Free Lands of Middle-earth
fell to the power of the Ring.</i>

31
00:02:23,477 --> 00:02:26,521
<i>But there were some who resisted.</i>

32
00:02:26,980 --> 00:02:31,652
<i>A Last Alliance of Men and Elves
marched against the armies of Mordor.</i>

33
00:02:31,860 --> 00:02:36,490
<i>And on the slopes of Mount Doom, they
fought for the freedom of Middle-earth.</i>

34
00:02:43,086 --> 00:02:46,977
{\an8}[CHORUS IN ADÛNAIC]: <i> We take unto ourselves
<font color="#bdaa00">(Nênâkham nêpâm)</font></i>

35
00:02:48,550 --> 00:02:53,930
{\an8}<i>the power and glory
<font color="#bdaa00">([a]bârat-aglar)</font></i>

36
00:02:49,294 --> 00:02:50,347
[IN SINDARIN] Hold positions!
<font color="#00bd00">(Tangado haid!)</font>

37
00:02:51,847 --> 00:02:53,647
Release the arrows!
<font color="#00bd00">(Leithio i philinn!)</font>

38
00:02:54,051 --> 00:02:57,825
{\an8}<i>The Lords of Unending Life
<font color="#bdaa00">(Nêbâ Katharâd)</font></i>

39
00:02:54,149 --> 00:02:54,971
Positions!
<font color="#00bd00">(Haid!)</font>

40
00:02:59,470 --> 00:03:04,820
{\an8}<i>We are the Nine
<font color="#bdaa00">(Nidir nênâ)</font></i>

41
00:03:04,844 --> 00:03:11,988
{\an8}<i>We renounce the darkness
<font color="#bdaa00">(Nêbîtham [dâ]ur)</font></i>

42
00:03:06,812 --> 00:03:09,439
<i>Victory was near.</i>

43
00:03:14,194 --> 00:03:15,946
<i>But the power of the Ring...</i>

44
00:03:16,780 --> 00:03:18,198
<i>...could not be undone.</i>

45
00:03:27,128 --> 00:03:31,058
{\an8}<i>We take unto ourselves
<font color="#bdaa00">(Nênâkham nêpâm)</font></i>

46
00:03:32,780 --> 00:03:38,945
{\an8}<i>the power and glory
<font color="#bdaa00">([a]bârat-aglar)</font></i>

47
00:03:42,806 --> 00:03:44,725
<i>It was in this moment...</i>

48
00:03:44,933 --> 00:03:47,310
<i>...when all hope had faded...</i>

49
00:03:47,519 --> 00:03:51,648
<i>...that Isildur, son of the king,
took up his father's sword.</i>

50
00:04:22,721 --> 00:04:29,227
<i>Sauron, the enemy of the Free Peoples
of Middle-earth, was defeated.</i>

51
00:04:36,109 --> 00:04:38,278
<i>The Ring passed to Isildur...</i>

52
00:04:38,487 --> 00:04:42,699
<i>...who had this one chance
to destroy evil forever.</i>

53
00:04:43,408 --> 00:04:45,535
<i>But the hearts of Men...</i>

54
00:04:45,744 --> 00:04:48,246
<i>...are easily corrupted.</i>

55
00:04:48,497 --> 00:04:53,126
<i>And the Ring of Power
has a will of its own.</i>

56
00:05:18,318 --> 00:05:20,946
<i>It betrayed Isildur...</i>

57
00:05:22,781 --> 00:05:25,200
<i>...to his death.</i>

58
00:05:29,371 --> 00:05:33,250
<i>And some things
that should not have been forgotten...</i>

59
00:05:33,458 --> 00:05:35,794
<i>...were lost.</i>

60
00:05:36,628 --> 00:05:38,839
<i>History became legend...</i>

61
00:05:39,047 --> 00:05:41,049
<i>...legend became myth.</i>

62
00:05:41,258 --> 00:05:44,135
<i>And for
two and a half thousand years...</i>

63
00:05:44,302 --> 00:05:48,014
<i>...the Ring passed
out of all knowledge.</i>

64
00:05:48,640 --> 00:05:51,476
<i>Until, when chance came...</i>

65
00:05:52,143 --> 00:05:55,272
<i>...it ensnared a new bearer.</i>

66
00:05:56,606 --> 00:06:01,444
GOLLUM:
My precious.

67
00:06:01,695 --> 00:06:04,239
GALADRIEL: <i> The Ring came
to the creature Gollum...</i>

68
00:06:04,406 --> 00:06:08,326
<i>...who took it deep into the tunnels
of the Misty Mountains.</i>

69
00:06:08,618 --> 00:06:11,496
<i>And there it consumed him.</i>

70
00:06:11,746 --> 00:06:13,790
GOLLUM:
It came to me.

71
00:06:13,999 --> 00:06:18,420
My own. My love. My own.

72
00:06:18,628 --> 00:06:23,341
My precious.

73
00:06:26,970 --> 00:06:30,390
GALADRIEL: <i> The Ring brought
to Gollum unnatural long life.</i>

74
00:06:30,599 --> 00:06:34,436
<i>For 500 years it poisoned his mind.</i>

75
00:06:34,644 --> 00:06:39,232
<i>And in the gloom of Gollum's cave,
it waited.</i>

76
00:06:39,441 --> 00:06:42,694
<i>Darkness crept back
into the forests of the world.</i>

77
00:06:42,944 --> 00:06:45,780
<i>Rumor grew of a shadow in the East...</i>

78
00:06:45,989 --> 00:06:48,783
<i>...whispers of a nameless fear.</i>

79
00:06:48,992 --> 00:06:52,287
<i>And the Ring of Power perceived...</i>

80
00:06:52,495 --> 00:06:55,290
<i>...its time had now come.</i>

81
00:06:57,709 --> 00:07:00,378
<i>It abandoned Gollum.</i>

82
00:07:01,046 --> 00:07:05,550
<i>But something happened then
the Ring did not intend.</i>

83
00:07:06,384 --> 00:07:10,972
<i>It was picked up by the most unlikely
creature imaginable.</i>

84
00:07:11,181 --> 00:07:12,223
BILBO:
What's this?

85
00:07:12,432 --> 00:07:13,892
GALADRIEL:
<i>A Hobbit.</i>

86
00:07:14,059 --> 00:07:16,811
<i>Bilbo Baggins of the Shire.</i>

87
00:07:17,020 --> 00:07:18,772
A ring.

88
00:07:18,980 --> 00:07:20,857
GOLLUM:
Lost!

89
00:07:23,610 --> 00:07:27,072
My precious is lost!

90
00:07:27,280 --> 00:07:29,574
GALADRIEL:
<i>For the time will soon come...</i>

91
00:07:29,824 --> 00:07:34,996
<i>...when Hobbits will shape
the fortunes of all.</i>

92
00:07:39,751 --> 00:07:42,837
BILBO:
The 22nd day of September...

93
00:07:43,004 --> 00:07:44,214
...in the year 1400...

94
00:07:46,424 --> 00:07:48,051
...by Shire-reckoning.

95
00:07:49,427 --> 00:07:54,140
Bag End, Bagshot Row, Hobbiton,
Westfarthing...

96
00:07:55,517 --> 00:07:56,893
...the Shire...

97
00:07:57,060 --> 00:07:59,896
...Middle-earth.

98
00:08:04,526 --> 00:08:07,862
The Third Age of this world.

99
00:08:19,416 --> 00:08:23,420
<i>There and Back Again:</i>

100
00:08:23,962 --> 00:08:25,797
<i>A Hobbit's Tale.</i>

101
00:08:25,964 --> 00:08:28,466
By Bilbo Baggins.

102
00:08:34,723 --> 00:08:36,474
Now...

103
00:08:37,183 --> 00:08:39,185
...where to begin?

104
00:08:40,478 --> 00:08:41,521
Ah, yes...

105
00:08:45,984 --> 00:08:47,694
"Concerning...

106
00:08:49,362 --> 00:08:50,530
...Hobbits."

107
00:08:51,656 --> 00:08:55,201
<i>Hobbits have been living and farming
in the four Farthings of the Shire...</i>

108
00:08:55,368 --> 00:08:57,370
<i>...for many hundreds of years...</i>

109
00:08:57,537 --> 00:09:00,498
<i>...quite content to ignore
and be ignored...</i>

110
00:09:00,707 --> 00:09:03,877
<i>...by the world of the Big Folk.</i>

111
00:09:04,210 --> 00:09:09,883
<i>Middle-earth being, after all,
full of strange creatures beyond count...</i>

112
00:09:10,050 --> 00:09:13,219
<i>...Hobbits must seem
of little importance...</i>

113
00:09:13,386 --> 00:09:17,432
<i>...being neither renowned
as great warriors...</i>

114
00:09:17,599 --> 00:09:21,811
<i>...nor counted among the very wise.</i>

115
00:09:23,313 --> 00:09:25,774
[KNOCKING]

116
00:09:26,191 --> 00:09:29,194
Frodo! Someone at the door.

117
00:09:30,403 --> 00:09:32,947
<i>In fact, it has been remarked by some...</i>

118
00:09:33,198 --> 00:09:37,660
<i>...that Hobbits' only real passion
is for food.</i>

119
00:09:37,994 --> 00:09:40,205
<i>A rather unfair observation...</i>

120
00:09:40,371 --> 00:09:44,084
<i>...as we have also developed a keen
interest in the brewing of ales...</i>

121
00:09:44,501 --> 00:09:47,212
<i>...and the smoking of pipe-weed.</i>

122
00:09:47,670 --> 00:09:50,507
<i>But where our hearts truly lie...</i>

123
00:09:50,673 --> 00:09:52,842
<i>...is in peace and quiet...</i>

124
00:09:53,510 --> 00:09:55,678
<i>...and good, tilled earth.</i>

125
00:09:55,845 --> 00:10:01,059
<i>For all Hobbits share a love
of things that grow.</i>

126
00:10:04,187 --> 00:10:08,608
<i>And, yes, no doubt to others,
our ways seem quaint.</i>

127
00:10:08,817 --> 00:10:14,030
<i>But today of all days,
it is brought home to me:</i>

128
00:10:14,614 --> 00:10:20,495
<i>It is no bad thing
to celebrate a simple life.</i>

129
00:10:22,247 --> 00:10:23,623
[KNOCKING]

130
00:10:24,707 --> 00:10:27,877
Frodo, the door!

131
00:10:31,714 --> 00:10:32,924
Sticklebacks. Where is that boy?

132
00:10:33,883 --> 00:10:35,552
Frodo!

133
00:10:41,391 --> 00:10:44,894
MALE VOICE:
<i>Down from the door where it began</i>

134
00:10:46,563 --> 00:10:48,940
[WAGON RUMBLES]

135
00:10:49,607 --> 00:10:53,403
<i>And I must follow if I can</i>

136
00:10:54,404 --> 00:10:58,491
<i>The road goes ever on and on</i>

137
00:10:58,741 --> 00:11:02,245
<i>Down from the door where it began</i>

138
00:11:02,412 --> 00:11:07,375
<i>Now far ahead the road has gone</i>

139
00:11:08,001 --> 00:11:11,796
<i>-And I must follow if I can</i>
-You're late.

140
00:11:15,091 --> 00:11:18,887
A wizard is never late, Frodo Baggins.

141
00:11:19,637 --> 00:11:24,309
Nor is he early. He arrives
precisely when he means to.

142
00:11:35,653 --> 00:11:38,781
It's wonderful to see you, Gandalf!

143
00:11:42,619 --> 00:11:46,331
You didn't think I'd miss
your Uncle Bilbo's birthday?

144
00:11:47,999 --> 00:11:50,168
How is the old rascal?

145
00:11:50,668 --> 00:11:54,214
I hear it's going to be a party
of special magnificence.

146
00:11:54,422 --> 00:11:56,841
You know Bilbo.
He's got the whole place in an uproar.

147
00:11:57,008 --> 00:11:59,010
Well, that should please him.

148
00:11:59,177 --> 00:12:01,012
Half the Shire's been invited.

149
00:12:01,304 --> 00:12:03,932
And the rest of them are turning up
anyway.

150
00:12:07,060 --> 00:12:10,396
BILBO:
<i>And so life in the Shire goes on...</i>

151
00:12:10,563 --> 00:12:13,650
<i>...very much as it has
this past Age...</i>

152
00:12:13,816 --> 00:12:19,364
<i>...full of its own comings and goings,
with change coming slowly.</i>

153
00:12:19,530 --> 00:12:21,449
<i>If it comes at all.</i>

154
00:12:22,700 --> 00:12:26,162
<i>For things are made to endure
in the Shire...</i>

155
00:12:26,329 --> 00:12:29,832
<i>...passing from one generation
to the next.</i>

156
00:12:30,208 --> 00:12:35,213
<i>There's always been a Baggins
living here under the Hill...</i>

157
00:12:35,380 --> 00:12:36,714
<i>...in Bag End.</i>

158
00:12:39,509 --> 00:12:42,345
And there always will be.

159
00:12:43,012 --> 00:12:46,391
To tell you the truth,
Bilbo's been a bit odd lately.

160
00:12:47,850 --> 00:12:50,019
I mean, more than usual.

161
00:12:51,020 --> 00:12:52,981
He's taken to locking himself
in his study.

162
00:12:54,524 --> 00:12:58,695
<i>He spends hours poring over old maps
when he thinks I'm not looking.</i>

163
00:13:11,374 --> 00:13:13,042
Where's it gone?

164
00:13:39,569 --> 00:13:41,904
He's up to something.

165
00:13:50,038 --> 00:13:52,540
-All right, then. Keep your secrets.
-What?

166
00:13:52,749 --> 00:13:54,417
But I know you have something
to do with it.

167
00:13:54,625 --> 00:13:55,752
Good gracious me.

168
00:13:55,960 --> 00:13:58,254
Before you came along, we Bagginses
were very well thought of.

169
00:13:59,088 --> 00:14:00,089
Indeed.

170
00:14:00,423 --> 00:14:02,592
Never had any adventures
or did anything unexpected.

171
00:14:03,176 --> 00:14:09,098
If you're referring to the incident
with the dragon, I was barely involved.

172
00:14:09,265 --> 00:14:12,852
All I did was give your uncle
a little nudge out of the door.

173
00:14:13,061 --> 00:14:17,106
Whatever you did, you've been officially
labeled a disturber of the peace.

174
00:14:17,565 --> 00:14:19,442
Oh, really?

175
00:14:25,073 --> 00:14:27,033
Gandalf! Gandalf!

176
00:14:27,742 --> 00:14:30,620
[CHILDREN SHOUTING]

177
00:14:33,122 --> 00:14:34,374
FEMALE HOBBIT 1:
Fireworks, Gandalf!

178
00:14:37,460 --> 00:14:40,046
FEMALE HOBBIT 2: Gandalf!
MALE HOBBIT: Fireworks, Gandalf!

179
00:14:58,898 --> 00:14:59,941
Gandalf?

180
00:15:00,483 --> 00:15:04,612
-I'm glad you're back.
-So am I, dear boy.

181
00:15:09,075 --> 00:15:10,827
So am I.

182
00:15:28,970 --> 00:15:31,472
Whoa, whoa.

183
00:15:42,692 --> 00:15:44,193
BILBO:
No, thank you!

184
00:15:44,360 --> 00:15:48,322
We don't want any more visitors,
well-wishers or distant relations!

185
00:15:48,531 --> 00:15:52,034
And what about very old friends?

186
00:15:55,204 --> 00:15:56,873
Gandalf?

187
00:15:57,540 --> 00:16:01,043
-Bilbo Baggins.
-My dear Gandalf!

188
00:16:01,210 --> 00:16:06,382
Good to see you. 111 years old!
Who would believe it?

189
00:16:08,134 --> 00:16:10,136
You haven't aged a day.

190
00:16:16,726 --> 00:16:18,728
Come on, come in!

191
00:16:18,895 --> 00:16:21,355
Welcome, welcome.

192
00:16:22,523 --> 00:16:25,067
Oh, here we are.

193
00:16:26,736 --> 00:16:29,197
Tea? Or maybe something
a little stronger?

194
00:16:29,363 --> 00:16:33,159
I've got a few bottles
of the Old Winyard left. 1296.

195
00:16:33,367 --> 00:16:37,413
Very good year. Almost as old as I am.

196
00:16:38,581 --> 00:16:43,085
It was laid down by my father.
What say we open one, eh?

197
00:16:43,252 --> 00:16:45,922
Just tea, thank you.

198
00:16:50,259 --> 00:16:52,094
Oh!

199
00:16:52,261 --> 00:16:53,930
I was expecting you sometime
last week.

200
00:16:54,180 --> 00:16:57,433
Not that it matters. You come and go as
you please. Always have and always will.

201
00:16:57,683 --> 00:17:02,939
You caught me a bit unprepared. We've
only got cold chicken and a bit of pickle...

202
00:17:03,105 --> 00:17:06,442
There's some cheese here.
No, that won't do.

203
00:17:06,692 --> 00:17:10,613
We've got raspberry jam,
an apple tart...

204
00:17:11,280 --> 00:17:15,243
But not much for afters.
Oh, no, we're all right.

205
00:17:15,451 --> 00:17:18,287
I've just found some sponge cake.

206
00:17:21,207 --> 00:17:22,542
I could make you some eggs
if you'd--

207
00:17:26,295 --> 00:17:28,965
-Just tea, thank you.
-Oh, right.

208
00:17:30,132 --> 00:17:32,468
-You don't mind if I eat, do you?
-No, not at all.

209
00:17:32,635 --> 00:17:33,970
[KNOCKING]

210
00:17:34,178 --> 00:17:35,429
FEMALE HOBBIT:
Bilbo! Bilbo Baggins!

211
00:17:35,638 --> 00:17:37,223
I'm not at home!

212
00:17:43,229 --> 00:17:45,815
It's the Sackville-Bagginses.

213
00:17:45,982 --> 00:17:48,109
-I know you're in there!
-They're after the house.

214
00:17:48,776 --> 00:17:51,279
They've never forgiven me
for living this long.

215
00:17:51,487 --> 00:17:54,282
I've got to get away from these confounded
relatives, hanging on the bell all day...

216
00:17:54,448 --> 00:17:56,325
...never giving me a moment's peace.

217
00:17:57,118 --> 00:18:00,663
I want to see mountains again.
Mountains, Gandalf!

218
00:18:00,830 --> 00:18:05,334
And then find somewhere quiet
where I can finish my book. Oh, tea.

219
00:18:05,501 --> 00:18:09,505
-So you mean to go through with your plan?
-Yes, yes. It's all in hand.

220
00:18:09,672 --> 00:18:11,966
All the arrangements are made.

221
00:18:14,010 --> 00:18:15,511
Oh, thank you.

222
00:18:16,262 --> 00:18:18,347
Frodo suspects something.

223
00:18:18,514 --> 00:18:21,017
Of course he does. He's a Baggins...

224
00:18:21,267 --> 00:18:23,853
...not some block headed Bracegirdle
from Hardbottle.

225
00:18:24,353 --> 00:18:27,189
You will tell him, won't you?

226
00:18:28,024 --> 00:18:30,151
-Yes, yes.
-He's very fond of you.

227
00:18:32,361 --> 00:18:33,863
I know.

228
00:18:36,198 --> 00:18:39,535
He'd probably come with me
if I asked him.

229
00:18:40,202 --> 00:18:43,664
I think in his heart, Frodo's
still in love with the Shire.

230
00:18:45,207 --> 00:18:47,543
The woods, the fields.

231
00:18:47,710 --> 00:18:50,046
Little rivers.

232
00:18:54,550 --> 00:18:57,219
I am old, Gandalf.

233
00:18:58,554 --> 00:19:03,893
I know I don't look it, but I'm
beginning to feel it in my heart.

234
00:19:06,062 --> 00:19:08,564
I feel thin.

235
00:19:08,731 --> 00:19:10,399
Sort of stretched...

236
00:19:11,734 --> 00:19:15,071
...like butter scraped
over too much bread.

237
00:19:15,237 --> 00:19:19,742
I need a holiday. A very long holiday.

238
00:19:19,909 --> 00:19:23,204
And I don't expect I shall return.

239
00:19:25,414 --> 00:19:28,584
In fact, I mean not to.

240
00:19:31,253 --> 00:19:35,383
Old Toby. The finest weed
in the Southfarthing.

241
00:19:50,106 --> 00:19:51,732
Ah.

242
00:19:52,733 --> 00:19:55,277
Gandalf, my old friend...

243
00:19:55,444 --> 00:19:58,280
...this will be a night to remember.

244
00:19:59,865 --> 00:20:01,826
[CHEERING]

245
00:20:03,035 --> 00:20:06,122
[MUSIC PLAYS]

246
00:20:21,137 --> 00:20:22,138
BILBO:
Hello, hello.

247
00:20:22,471 --> 00:20:26,475
Fatty Bolger. Lovely to see you.
Welcome, welcome.

248
00:20:27,476 --> 00:20:30,104
Go on, Sam. Ask Rosie for a dance.

249
00:20:32,648 --> 00:20:36,277
-I think I'll just have another ale.
-Oh, no, you don't.

250
00:20:37,319 --> 00:20:39,113
Go on!

251
00:20:49,165 --> 00:20:51,000
So there I was...

252
00:20:51,292 --> 00:20:55,337
...at the mercy
of three monstrous trolls.

253
00:20:55,504 --> 00:20:57,506
And they were all arguing
amongst themselves...

254
00:20:57,673 --> 00:21:00,134
...about how they were
going to cook us.

255
00:21:00,342 --> 00:21:05,347
Whether it be turned on a spit, or to sit
on us one by one, squash us into jelly.

256
00:21:06,348 --> 00:21:09,935
They spent so much time arguing
the whithertos and the whyfors...

257
00:21:10,144 --> 00:21:13,689
...that the sun's first light
crept over the top of the trees...

258
00:21:14,690 --> 00:21:17,193
...and turned them all to stone!

259
00:21:18,277 --> 00:21:20,362
[LAUGHS]

260
00:21:22,490 --> 00:21:23,866
MERRY:
Quickly.

261
00:21:26,327 --> 00:21:27,828
Whoa!

262
00:21:28,037 --> 00:21:30,039
Up they go!

263
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:34,210
No, the big one.

264
00:21:43,385 --> 00:21:46,222
Mrs. Bracegirdle, how nice to see you.
Welcome, welcome.

265
00:21:46,388 --> 00:21:48,349
Are all these children yours?

266
00:21:48,516 --> 00:21:51,519
Good gracious,
you have been productive.

267
00:21:53,521 --> 00:21:54,855
FEMALE HOBBIT:
Bilbo?

268
00:21:56,565 --> 00:21:58,234
Sackville-Bagginses!

269
00:21:58,484 --> 00:21:59,568
Quickly, hide!

270
00:22:09,411 --> 00:22:11,580
Thank you, my boy.

271
00:22:13,082 --> 00:22:15,501
You're a good lad, Frodo.

272
00:22:16,710 --> 00:22:19,588
I'm very selfish, you know.

273
00:22:20,005 --> 00:22:23,425
Yes, I am. Very selfish.

274
00:22:23,592 --> 00:22:25,845
I don't know why I took you in
after your mother and father died...

275
00:22:26,011 --> 00:22:27,555
...but it wasn't out of charity.

276
00:22:28,264 --> 00:22:29,723
I think it was because...

277
00:22:29,890 --> 00:22:32,226
...of all my numerous relations...

278
00:22:32,518 --> 00:22:36,021
...you were the one Baggins
that showed real spirit.

279
00:22:36,272 --> 00:22:38,107
Bilbo, have you been
at the Gaffer's home brew?

280
00:22:38,274 --> 00:22:40,025
No.

281
00:22:40,276 --> 00:22:42,945
Well, yes, but that's not the point.

282
00:22:43,112 --> 00:22:46,407
The point is, Frodo...

283
00:22:49,451 --> 00:22:51,453
...you'll be all right.

284
00:22:54,790 --> 00:22:56,959
-Done!
-You're supposed to stick it in the ground.

285
00:22:57,126 --> 00:22:58,627
-It is in the ground.
-Outside!

286
00:22:58,794 --> 00:23:00,296
This was your idea.

287
00:23:16,145 --> 00:23:17,646
Bilbo.

288
00:23:18,814 --> 00:23:21,650
Bilbo, watch out for the dragon!

289
00:23:21,817 --> 00:23:25,154
Nonsense. There hasn't been a dragon
in these parts for a thousand years.

290
00:23:38,667 --> 00:23:42,338
-That was good.
-Let's get another one.

291
00:23:43,547 --> 00:23:48,093
GANDALF:
Meriadoc Brandybuck and Peregrin Took.

292
00:23:48,260 --> 00:23:50,137
I might've known.

293
00:23:56,018 --> 00:23:58,103
FEMALE HOBBIT:
Speech, Bilbo!

294
00:23:58,979 --> 00:24:00,314
MALE HOBBIT:
Speech!

295
00:24:00,522 --> 00:24:01,607
Speech!

296
00:24:06,862 --> 00:24:09,156
My dear Bagginses and Boffins...

297
00:24:09,949 --> 00:24:12,159
...Tooks and Brandybucks...

298
00:24:12,326 --> 00:24:14,828
...Grubbs, Chubbs...

299
00:24:15,037 --> 00:24:16,080
...Hornblowers...

300
00:24:17,206 --> 00:24:18,874
...Bolgers...

301
00:24:19,291 --> 00:24:20,834
...Bracegirdles...

302
00:24:21,043 --> 00:24:23,671
-...and Proudfoots.
-Proudfeet!

303
00:24:25,839 --> 00:24:29,009
Today is my 111th birthday!

304
00:24:30,803 --> 00:24:32,346
Happy birthday!

305
00:24:32,554 --> 00:24:36,850
But alas, eleventy-one years is
far too short a time to live among...

306
00:24:37,017 --> 00:24:39,895
...such excellent
and admirable Hobbits.

307
00:24:40,854 --> 00:24:43,565
I don't know half of you
half as well as I should like...

308
00:24:43,732 --> 00:24:48,362
...and I like less than half of you
half as well as you deserve.

309
00:24:51,865 --> 00:24:53,492
I, uh--

310
00:24:58,330 --> 00:25:00,708
I have things to do.

311
00:25:07,089 --> 00:25:09,216
I've put this off far too long.

312
00:25:13,053 --> 00:25:17,016
I regret to announce this is the end!

313
00:25:18,183 --> 00:25:19,351
I'm going now.

314
00:25:20,436 --> 00:25:23,355
I bid you all a very fond farewell.

315
00:25:25,733 --> 00:25:26,942
Goodbye.

316
00:25:32,781 --> 00:25:34,450
[HOBBITS CLAMORING]

317
00:25:36,618 --> 00:25:39,288
[FOOTSTEPS]

318
00:25:50,132 --> 00:25:52,217
[LAUGHS]

319
00:26:00,184 --> 00:26:03,312
I suppose you think
that was terribly clever.

320
00:26:03,479 --> 00:26:06,899
Come on, Gandalf.
Did you see their faces?

321
00:26:07,066 --> 00:26:12,112
There are many magic rings in this world,
and none of them should be used lightly.

322
00:26:12,321 --> 00:26:14,490
It was just a bit of fun.

323
00:26:14,698 --> 00:26:18,410
Oh, you're probably right, as usual.

324
00:26:19,787 --> 00:26:23,332
-You will keep an eye on Frodo, won't you?
-Two eyes.

325
00:26:23,499 --> 00:26:26,210
As often as I can spare them.

326
00:26:26,418 --> 00:26:29,588
-I'm leaving everything to him.
-What about this ring of yours?

327
00:26:29,797 --> 00:26:33,133
-Is that staying too?
-Yes, yes.

328
00:26:33,759 --> 00:26:37,638
It's in an envelope over there
on the mantelpiece.

329
00:26:38,722 --> 00:26:41,683
No. Wait, it's...

330
00:26:44,186 --> 00:26:46,855
...here in my pocket.

331
00:26:51,360 --> 00:26:54,738
Isn't that--? Isn't that odd, now?

332
00:26:56,365 --> 00:26:59,868
Yet, after all, why not?

333
00:27:01,453 --> 00:27:06,333
-Why shouldn't I keep it?
-I think you should leave the ring behind.

334
00:27:06,750 --> 00:27:08,961
Is that so hard?

335
00:27:09,128 --> 00:27:10,462
Well, no.

336
00:27:12,840 --> 00:27:14,383
And yes.

337
00:27:16,343 --> 00:27:19,388
Now it comes to it,
I don't feel like parting with it.

338
00:27:19,638 --> 00:27:21,390
It's mine. I found it! It came to me!

339
00:27:21,557 --> 00:27:25,811
-There's no need to get angry.
-Well, if I'm angry, it's your fault!

340
00:27:26,270 --> 00:27:28,063
It's mine.

341
00:27:29,314 --> 00:27:31,817
My own.

342
00:27:32,151 --> 00:27:36,155
-My precious.
-Precious?

343
00:27:36,321 --> 00:27:39,199
It's been called that before,
but not by you.

344
00:27:39,408 --> 00:27:41,994
What business is it of yours
what I do with my own things?

345
00:27:42,202 --> 00:27:44,913
I think you've had that ring
quite long enough.

346
00:27:45,164 --> 00:27:48,000
-You want it for yourself!
-Bilbo Baggins!

347
00:27:48,208 --> 00:27:52,421
Do not take me for some conjurer
of cheap tricks.

348
00:27:52,671 --> 00:27:56,341
I am not trying to rob you.

349
00:28:01,388 --> 00:28:03,098
I'm trying to help you.

350
00:28:04,433 --> 00:28:05,976
[BILBO WHIMPERS]

351
00:28:11,565 --> 00:28:14,902
All your long years,
we've been friends.

352
00:28:15,277 --> 00:28:17,446
Trust me as you once did.

353
00:28:19,281 --> 00:28:21,116
Let it go.

354
00:28:22,242 --> 00:28:24,661
You're right, Gandalf.

355
00:28:26,788 --> 00:28:29,458
The ring must go to Frodo.

356
00:28:30,792 --> 00:28:33,795
It's late. The road is long.

357
00:28:33,962 --> 00:28:36,465
Yes, it is time.

358
00:28:39,301 --> 00:28:41,303
-Bilbo.
-Hm?

359
00:28:41,803 --> 00:28:44,306
The ring is still in your pocket.

360
00:28:46,683 --> 00:28:48,602
Ah. Yes.

361
00:29:19,007 --> 00:29:22,010
I've thought up an ending for my book:

362
00:29:23,679 --> 00:29:28,684
"And he lived happily ever after
to the end of his days."

363
00:29:28,850 --> 00:29:32,312
And I'm sure you will, my dear friend.

364
00:29:33,355 --> 00:29:34,815
Goodbye, Gandalf.

365
00:29:37,317 --> 00:29:40,195
Goodbye, dear Bilbo.

366
00:29:47,995 --> 00:29:52,207
BILBO:
<i>The road goes ever on and on</i>

367
00:29:52,897 --> 00:29:56,126
<i>Down from the door where it began</i>

368
00:29:54,751 --> 00:29:57,129
Until our next meeting.
<i> </i>

369
00:30:24,531 --> 00:30:28,201
BILBO:
<i>It's mine. My own.</i>

370
00:30:28,368 --> 00:30:31,788
<i>My precious.</i>

371
00:30:32,080 --> 00:30:35,000
Riddles in the dark.

372
00:30:35,208 --> 00:30:36,626
Bilbo!

373
00:30:36,793 --> 00:30:38,378
Bilbo!

374
00:30:42,007 --> 00:30:44,926
My precious.

375
00:30:46,553 --> 00:30:48,764
Precious.

376
00:30:48,930 --> 00:30:51,516
He's gone, hasn't he?

377
00:30:54,269 --> 00:30:57,314
He talked for so long about leaving...

378
00:30:57,564 --> 00:31:00,275
...I didn't think he'd really do it.

379
00:31:04,738 --> 00:31:06,615
Gandalf?

380
00:31:14,915 --> 00:31:16,583
Bilbo's ring.

381
00:31:16,917 --> 00:31:19,294
He's gone to stay with the Elves.

382
00:31:19,461 --> 00:31:22,589
He's left you Bag End.

383
00:31:26,176 --> 00:31:28,762
Along with all his possessions.

384
00:31:28,929 --> 00:31:31,807
The ring is yours now.

385
00:31:34,434 --> 00:31:37,938
-Put it somewhere out of sight.
-Where are you going?

386
00:31:38,105 --> 00:31:40,357
-There are some things that I must see to.
-What things?

387
00:31:40,565 --> 00:31:44,820
-Questions. Questions that need answering.
-You've only just arrived.

388
00:31:45,695 --> 00:31:48,323
I don't understand.

389
00:31:51,660 --> 00:31:52,661
Neither do I.

390
00:31:55,956 --> 00:31:58,291
Keep it secret.

391
00:31:58,458 --> 00:32:00,210
Keep it safe.

392
00:32:32,617 --> 00:32:35,036
[GOLLUM SCREAMS]

393
00:32:35,203 --> 00:32:37,372
GOLLUM:
<i>Shire!</i>

394
00:32:37,706 --> 00:32:40,834
<i>Baggins!</i>

395
00:32:40,858 --> 00:32:49,708
{\an8}[CHORUS IN ADÛNAIC]: <i> We renounce our Maker.
<font color="#bdaa00">(Nêbâbîtham Magânanê)</font></i>

396
00:32:53,054 --> 00:32:55,640
[THUNDER RUMBLES]

397
00:33:29,382 --> 00:33:32,260
GANDALF:
<i>"The year 3434 of the Second Age.</i>

398
00:33:32,469 --> 00:33:36,890
<i>Here follows the account of Isildur,
High King of Gondor...</i>

399
00:33:37,090 --> 00:33:40,761
<i>...and the finding
of the Ring of Power."</i>

400
00:33:44,272 --> 00:33:46,107
<i>"It has come to me.</i>

401
00:33:46,274 --> 00:33:49,778
<i>The One Ring. It shall be
an heirloom of my kingdom.</i>

402
00:33:49,945 --> 00:33:53,406
<i>All those who follow in my bloodline
shall be bound to its fate...</i>

403
00:33:53,615 --> 00:33:57,410
<i>...for I will risk
no hurt to the Ring.</i>

404
00:33:57,619 --> 00:34:00,121
<i>It is precious to me...</i>

405
00:34:00,956 --> 00:34:03,625
<i>...though I buy it with great pain.</i>

406
00:34:05,099 --> 00:34:08,128
VOICE OF THE RING [WHISPERS IN BLACK SPEECH]: <i> Sauron...
<font color="#bd2600">(Zigur...)</font></i>

407
00:34:06,753 --> 00:34:10,966
<i>The markings upon the band
begin to fade.</i>

408
00:34:11,299 --> 00:34:15,971
<i>The writing, which at first was as clear
as red flame, has all but disappeared.</i>

409
00:34:16,221 --> 00:34:20,267
<i>A secret now
that only fire can tell."</i>

410
00:34:24,813 --> 00:34:26,648
[HOOVES CLOPPING]

411
00:34:36,783 --> 00:34:39,786
Shire.

412
00:34:39,953 --> 00:34:41,955
Baggins.

413
00:34:42,455 --> 00:34:46,501
There's no Bagginses around here.
They're all up in Hobbiton.

414
00:34:48,169 --> 00:34:49,671
That way.

415
00:34:55,677 --> 00:34:57,887
<i>To heal my heart and drown my woe</i>

416
00:34:58,054 --> 00:35:00,390
<i>Rain may fall and wind may blow</i>

417
00:35:00,557 --> 00:35:02,517
<i>But there still be</i>

418
00:35:02,684 --> 00:35:04,144
<i>Many miles to go</i>

419
00:35:04,352 --> 00:35:06,271
<i>Sweet is the sound of the pouring rain</i>

420
00:35:06,479 --> 00:35:08,648
<i>And the stream that falls
From hill to plain</i>

421
00:35:08,857 --> 00:35:10,692
<i>Better than rain or rippling brook</i>

422
00:35:10,859 --> 00:35:13,278
<i>Is a mug of beer inside this Took</i>

423
00:35:16,698 --> 00:35:19,534
There's been some strange folk
crossing the Shire.

424
00:35:19,993 --> 00:35:23,830
Dwarves and others of a less
than savory nature.

425
00:35:24,331 --> 00:35:25,707
War is brewing.

426
00:35:26,374 --> 00:35:29,210
The mountains are fair teeming
with goblins.

427
00:35:29,419 --> 00:35:32,047
Far-off tales and children's stories,
that's all that is.

428
00:35:32,213 --> 00:35:36,718
You're beginning to sound like that old
Bilbo Baggins. Cracked, he was.

429
00:35:36,885 --> 00:35:39,888
Young Mr. Frodo here,
he's cracking.

430
00:35:40,055 --> 00:35:41,514
And proud of it.

431
00:35:41,681 --> 00:35:43,933
-Cheers, Gaffer.
-Cheers.

432
00:35:44,100 --> 00:35:48,229
It's none of our concern what goes on
beyond our borders.

433
00:35:48,396 --> 00:35:52,734
Keep your nose out of trouble,
and no trouble'll come to you.

434
00:35:56,071 --> 00:35:58,281
-Good night, lads.
-Good night.

435
00:35:58,448 --> 00:36:02,952
Good night, sweet maiden
of the golden ale.

436
00:36:03,119 --> 00:36:05,538
Mind who you're sweet-talking.

437
00:36:05,705 --> 00:36:10,251
Don't worry, Sam. Rosie knows an idiot
when she sees one.

438
00:36:11,252 --> 00:36:12,420
Does she?

439
00:36:13,088 --> 00:36:16,091
-Good night, Sam.
-Good night, Mr. Frodo.

440
00:36:40,865 --> 00:36:43,368
Is it secret? Is it safe?

441
00:36:45,954 --> 00:36:47,872
[PIG SQUEALS]

442
00:36:49,124 --> 00:36:50,583
Ah.

443
00:36:52,252 --> 00:36:54,379
What are you doing?

444
00:37:06,975 --> 00:37:09,477
Hold out your hand, Frodo.

445
00:37:09,644 --> 00:37:10,812
It's quite cool.

446
00:37:14,399 --> 00:37:16,151
What can you see?

447
00:37:17,986 --> 00:37:20,321
Can you see anything?

448
00:37:23,032 --> 00:37:24,492
Nothing.

449
00:37:25,118 --> 00:37:27,120
There's nothing.

450
00:37:28,163 --> 00:37:29,664
Wait.

451
00:37:31,554 --> 00:37:34,334
THE RING [WHISPERS IN BLACK SPEECH]: <i> Sauron...
<font color="#bd2600">(Zigur...)</font></i>

452
00:37:33,793 --> 00:37:36,004
There are markings.

453
00:37:37,505 --> 00:37:40,925
It's some form of Elvish.
I can't read it.

454
00:37:41,134 --> 00:37:43,678
There are few who can.

455
00:37:44,220 --> 00:37:49,058
The language is that of Mordor,
which I will not utter here.

456
00:37:49,684 --> 00:37:50,727
Mordor!

457
00:37:51,019 --> 00:37:53,021
In the common tongue, it says:

458
00:37:53,229 --> 00:37:56,733
"One Ring to rule them all...

459
00:37:57,025 --> 00:37:59,319
...One Ring to find them...

460
00:37:59,527 --> 00:38:01,696
...One Ring to bring them all...

461
00:38:02,030 --> 00:38:05,033
...and in the darkness bind them."

462
00:38:06,659 --> 00:38:08,703
This is the One Ring...

463
00:38:08,870 --> 00:38:14,167
...forged by the Dark Lord Sauron
in the fires of Mount Doom.

464
00:38:14,375 --> 00:38:18,379
Taken by Isildur
from the hand of Sauron himself.

465
00:38:19,172 --> 00:38:21,716
Bilbo found it.

466
00:38:22,175 --> 00:38:24,093
-In Gollum's cave.
-Yes.

467
00:38:24,344 --> 00:38:28,890
For 60 years, the Ring lay quiet
in Bilbo's keeping...

468
00:38:29,057 --> 00:38:32,477
...prolonging his life,
delaying old age.

469
00:38:33,102 --> 00:38:37,565
But no longer, Frodo.
Evil is stirring in Mordor.

470
00:38:37,732 --> 00:38:40,109
The Ring has awoken.

471
00:38:40,360 --> 00:38:43,071
It's heard its master's call.

472
00:38:43,279 --> 00:38:47,200
But he was destroyed.
Sauron was destroyed.

473
00:38:47,929 --> 00:38:50,578
THE RING: <i> Sauron...
<font color="#bd2600">(Zigur...)</font></i>

474
00:38:52,914 --> 00:38:54,999
GANDALF:
No, Frodo.

475
00:38:55,917 --> 00:38:59,254
The spirit of Sauron endured.

476
00:38:59,420 --> 00:39:04,759
His life force is bound to the Ring,
and the Ring survived.

477
00:39:05,093 --> 00:39:07,262
Sauron has returned.

478
00:39:08,137 --> 00:39:10,265
His Orcs have multiplied.

479
00:39:10,431 --> 00:39:14,477
His fortress at Barad-dûr
is rebuilt in the land of Mordor.

480
00:39:14,644 --> 00:39:19,440
Sauron needs only this Ring to cover
all the lands in a second darkness.

481
00:39:19,649 --> 00:39:21,734
He is seeking it.

482
00:39:21,943 --> 00:39:25,780
Seeking it. All his thought
is bent on it.

483
00:39:26,030 --> 00:39:28,741
For the Ring yearns above all else...

484
00:39:28,950 --> 00:39:32,328
...to return to the hand
of its master.

485
00:39:32,620 --> 00:39:34,330
They are one...

486
00:39:34,539 --> 00:39:37,625
...the Ring and the Dark Lord.

487
00:39:37,792 --> 00:39:38,835
Frodo...

488
00:39:39,419 --> 00:39:41,296
...he must never find it.

489
00:39:41,462 --> 00:39:42,547
FRODO:
All right.

490
00:39:42,839 --> 00:39:47,176
We put it away. We keep it hidden.
We never speak of it again.

491
00:39:47,343 --> 00:39:50,054
No one knows it's here, do they?

492
00:39:55,685 --> 00:39:56,936
Do they, Gandalf?

493
00:39:57,979 --> 00:40:01,357
There is one other who knew
that Bilbo had the Ring.

494
00:40:02,650 --> 00:40:05,653
I looked everywhere
for the creature Gollum.

495
00:40:05,820 --> 00:40:07,989
But the enemy found him first.

496
00:40:08,197 --> 00:40:09,532
[GOLLUM SCREAMS]

497
00:40:09,699 --> 00:40:12,201
GANDALF: <i> I don't know how long
they tortured him.</i>

498
00:40:12,368 --> 00:40:16,873
<i>But amidst the endless screams and
inane babble, they discerned two words:</i>

499
00:40:17,081 --> 00:40:19,208
GOLLUM:
Shire!

500
00:40:19,375 --> 00:40:21,002
Baggins!

501
00:40:21,210 --> 00:40:23,046
Shire.

502
00:40:23,212 --> 00:40:26,174
Baggins. But that would
lead them here!

503
00:40:28,843 --> 00:40:30,011
Who goes there?

504
00:40:31,721 --> 00:40:32,972
Take it, Gandalf!

505
00:40:33,348 --> 00:40:34,390
-Take it!
-No, Frodo.

506
00:40:34,599 --> 00:40:36,976
-You must take it!
-You cannot offer me this ring!

507
00:40:37,185 --> 00:40:40,521
-I'm giving it to you!
-Don't tempt me, Frodo!

508
00:40:42,023 --> 00:40:44,233
I dare not take it.

509
00:40:44,609 --> 00:40:47,028
Not even to keep it safe.

510
00:40:48,196 --> 00:40:50,198
Understand, Frodo...

511
00:40:50,865 --> 00:40:54,494
...I would use this Ring
from a desire to do good.

512
00:40:59,874 --> 00:41:05,630
But through me, it would wield a power
too great and terrible to imagine.

513
00:41:06,214 --> 00:41:09,133
-But it cannot stay in the Shire!
-No.

514
00:41:11,010 --> 00:41:12,637
No, it can't.

515
00:41:17,934 --> 00:41:19,352
What must I do?

516
00:41:21,020 --> 00:41:24,565
-You must leave. And leave quickly.
-Where? Where do I go?

517
00:41:24,732 --> 00:41:28,027
Get out of the Shire.
Make for the village of Bree.

518
00:41:28,277 --> 00:41:29,404
Bree.

519
00:41:29,570 --> 00:41:32,365
-What about you?
-I'll be waiting for you...

520
00:41:32,573 --> 00:41:35,034
...at the inn of the Prancing Pony.

521
00:41:35,243 --> 00:41:38,955
-And the Ring will be safe there?
- I don't know, Frodo.

522
00:41:39,163 --> 00:41:41,165
I don't have any answers.

523
00:41:42,667 --> 00:41:48,256
I must see the head of my order. He is
both wise and powerful. Trust me, Frodo.

524
00:41:48,423 --> 00:41:50,550
He'll know what to do.

525
00:41:51,175 --> 00:41:53,970
You'll have to leave the name
of Baggins behind you.

526
00:41:54,262 --> 00:41:56,764
That name is not safe
outside the Shire.

527
00:41:57,390 --> 00:42:00,685
Travel only by day.
And stay off the road.

528
00:42:01,310 --> 00:42:04,480
I can cut across country
easily enough.

529
00:42:06,983 --> 00:42:08,317
My dear Frodo.

530
00:42:08,609 --> 00:42:11,654
Hobbits really are amazing creatures.

531
00:42:11,821 --> 00:42:14,782
You can learn all that there is to
know about their ways in a month.

532
00:42:14,949 --> 00:42:17,326
And yet, after a hundred years...

533
00:42:17,493 --> 00:42:19,579
...they can still surprise you.

534
00:42:19,787 --> 00:42:20,955
[RUSTLING]

535
00:42:21,205 --> 00:42:22,498
Get down.

536
00:42:31,132 --> 00:42:32,258
[GROANING]

537
00:42:34,802 --> 00:42:38,264
Confound it all, Samwise Gamgee!
Have you been eavesdropping?

538
00:42:38,431 --> 00:42:42,935
I haven't been dropping no eaves. Honest.
I was cutting the grass under the window.

539
00:42:43,102 --> 00:42:45,521
A little late for trimming the verge,
don't you think?

540
00:42:45,730 --> 00:42:48,608
-I heard raised voices.
-What did you hear? Speak!

541
00:42:48,816 --> 00:42:49,859
Nothing important.

542
00:42:50,443 --> 00:42:54,530
That is, I heard a good deal about a ring,
a Dark Lord and the end of the world but--

543
00:42:54,739 --> 00:42:59,494
Please, Mr. Gandalf, sir, don't hurt me.
Don't turn me into anything unnatural.

544
00:43:00,161 --> 00:43:01,829
No?

545
00:43:02,997 --> 00:43:04,165
Perhaps not.

546
00:43:05,374 --> 00:43:08,836
I've thought of a better use for you.

547
00:43:10,546 --> 00:43:13,549
GANDALF:
Come along, Samwise. Keep up.

548
00:43:15,051 --> 00:43:17,345
Be careful, both of you.

549
00:43:17,553 --> 00:43:20,348
The enemy has many spies
in his service:

550
00:43:20,556 --> 00:43:23,518
Birds, beasts.

551
00:43:25,269 --> 00:43:27,063
Is it safe?

552
00:43:28,773 --> 00:43:30,149
Never put it on...

553
00:43:30,358 --> 00:43:33,736
...for the agents of the Dark Lord
will be drawn to its power.

554
00:43:33,903 --> 00:43:35,404
Always remember, Frodo...

555
00:43:35,905 --> 00:43:39,075
...the Ring is trying to get back
to its master.

556
00:43:39,492 --> 00:43:41,577
It wants to be found.

557
00:43:49,043 --> 00:43:51,796
[BIRDS SQUAWKING]

558
00:44:22,201 --> 00:44:24,412
This is it.

559
00:44:24,745 --> 00:44:26,914
This is what?

560
00:44:27,206 --> 00:44:29,250
If I take one more step...

561
00:44:29,750 --> 00:44:33,629
...it'll be the farthest away
from home I've ever been.

562
00:44:37,925 --> 00:44:39,427
Come on, Sam.

563
00:44:47,852 --> 00:44:49,645
Remember what Bilbo used to say:

564
00:44:50,229 --> 00:44:53,983
-"It's a dangerous business, Frodo."
BILBO: <i>"Going out your door.</i>

565
00:44:54,150 --> 00:44:58,613
<i>You step onto the road,
and if you don't keep your feet...</i>

566
00:44:58,779 --> 00:45:02,950
<i>...there's no knowing where
you might be swept off to."</i>

567
00:45:09,002 --> 00:45:16,807
{\an8}[WOOD-ELVES SING IN SINDARIN]:
<i>O Queen beyond the Western Seas!
<font color="#00bd00">(Rîn athar annún-aearath!)</font></i>

568
00:45:16,964 --> 00:45:17,907
Sam.

569
00:45:18,251 --> 00:45:26,708
{\an8}<i>O light to us that wander
<font color="#00bd00">(Calad ammen i reniar)</font></i>

570
00:45:22,303 --> 00:45:23,429
Wood-elves.

571
00:45:28,008 --> 00:45:36,457
{\an8}<i>Amid the tree-woven lands of Middle-earth.
<font color="#00bd00">(Mi 'aladhremmin ennorath.)</font></i>

572
00:45:37,151 --> 00:45:39,525
They're going to the harbor
beyond the White Towers.

573
00:45:38,119 --> 00:45:47,009
{\an8}<i>O Elbereth Star-kindler!
<font color="#00bd00">(A Elbereth Gilthoniel!)</font></i>

574
00:45:41,197 --> 00:45:42,664
To the Grey Havens.

575
00:45:43,574 --> 00:45:45,618
SAM:
They're leaving Middle-earth.

576
00:45:45,785 --> 00:45:47,333
FRODO:
Never to return.

577
00:45:47,763 --> 00:45:56,648
{\an8}<i>Your eyes and breath like shining jewels
<font color="#00bd00">(I chîn a thûl lín míriel)</font></i>

578
00:45:50,873 --> 00:45:52,089
I don't know why...

579
00:45:53,668 --> 00:45:56,087
...it makes me sad.

580
00:45:58,172 --> 00:46:02,802
Everywhere I lie there's a dirty
great root sticking into my back.

581
00:46:03,511 --> 00:46:05,221
Just shut your eyes...

582
00:46:05,388 --> 00:46:08,182
...and imagine you're back
in your own bed...

583
00:46:08,349 --> 00:46:12,311
...with a soft mattress
and a lovely feather pillow.

584
00:46:21,612 --> 00:46:24,323
It's not working, Mr. Frodo.

585
00:46:24,490 --> 00:46:27,368
I'm never going to be able
to sleep out here.

586
00:46:29,704 --> 00:46:32,039
Me neither, Sam.

587
00:47:00,568 --> 00:47:03,612
MALE VOICE: <i> Smoke rises
from the Mountain of Doom.</i>

588
00:47:03,779 --> 00:47:05,448
<i>The hour grows late.</i>

589
00:47:05,656 --> 00:47:09,243
<i>And Gandalf the Grey
rides to Isengard...</i>

590
00:47:09,410 --> 00:47:11,871
<i>...seeking my counsel.</i>

591
00:47:12,079 --> 00:47:16,083
For that is why you have come,
is it not?

592
00:47:16,250 --> 00:47:17,543
My old friend.

593
00:47:17,793 --> 00:47:19,420
Saruman.

594
00:47:24,216 --> 00:47:27,261
SARUMAN: You are sure of this?
GANDALF: Beyond any doubt.

595
00:47:28,054 --> 00:47:30,306
So the Ring of Power has been found.

596
00:47:30,473 --> 00:47:33,726
All these long years,
it was in the Shire.

597
00:47:33,893 --> 00:47:37,063
-Under my very nose.
-Yet you did not have the wit to see it.

598
00:47:37,688 --> 00:47:42,193
Your love of the halfling's leaf
has clearly slowed your mind.

599
00:47:43,069 --> 00:47:47,073
But we still have time. Time enough
to counter Sauron if we act quickly.

600
00:47:47,239 --> 00:47:48,699
Time?

601
00:47:49,617 --> 00:47:52,244
What time do you think we have?

602
00:47:52,703 --> 00:47:56,582
Sauron has regained
much of his former strength.

603
00:47:56,749 --> 00:47:58,959
He cannot yet take physical form...

604
00:47:59,210 --> 00:48:01,921
...but his spirit has lost
none of its potency.

605
00:48:02,588 --> 00:48:07,635
Concealed within his fortress,
the Lord of Mordor sees all.

606
00:48:08,219 --> 00:48:14,141
His gaze pierces cloud, shadow,
earth and flesh.

607
00:48:15,643 --> 00:48:18,813
You know of what I speak, Gandalf.

608
00:48:19,730 --> 00:48:24,985
A Great Eye, lidless,
wreathed in flame.

609
00:48:25,945 --> 00:48:27,738
The Eye of Sauron.

610
00:48:27,947 --> 00:48:30,533
He is gathering all evil to him.

611
00:48:30,741 --> 00:48:33,244
Very soon, he'll have summoned
an army great enough...

612
00:48:33,411 --> 00:48:35,621
...for an assault upon Middle-earth.

613
00:48:35,955 --> 00:48:38,332
You know this?

614
00:48:38,833 --> 00:48:40,334
How?

615
00:48:40,960 --> 00:48:42,628
I have seen it.

616
00:48:43,045 --> 00:48:46,257
A palantír is a dangerous tool,
Saruman.

617
00:48:46,966 --> 00:48:48,467
Why?

618
00:48:48,926 --> 00:48:51,637
Why should we fear to use it?

619
00:48:54,265 --> 00:48:58,185
They are not all accounted for,
the lost Seeing-stones.

620
00:48:58,352 --> 00:49:01,605
We do not know who else
may be watching.

621
00:49:04,191 --> 00:49:06,944
The hour is later than you think.

622
00:49:07,111 --> 00:49:09,447
Sauron's forces are already moving.

623
00:49:11,699 --> 00:49:14,452
The Nine have left Minas Morgul.

624
00:49:14,827 --> 00:49:15,870
The Nine?

625
00:49:16,036 --> 00:49:19,123
They crossed the River Isen
on Midsummer's Eve...

626
00:49:19,290 --> 00:49:21,959
...disguised as riders in black.

627
00:49:22,168 --> 00:49:26,130
-They've reached the Shire?
-They will find the Ring.

628
00:49:27,715 --> 00:49:29,967
And kill the one who carries it.

629
00:49:30,468 --> 00:49:31,969
Frodo!

630
00:49:44,565 --> 00:49:48,986
You did not seriously think that a Hobbit
could contend with the will of Sauron?

631
00:49:49,737 --> 00:49:52,531
There are none who can.

632
00:49:55,034 --> 00:49:57,745
Against the power of Mordor...

633
00:49:57,912 --> 00:50:00,581
...there can be no victory.

634
00:50:02,541 --> 00:50:05,711
We must join with him, Gandalf.

635
00:50:07,004 --> 00:50:09,340
We must join with Sauron.

636
00:50:12,009 --> 00:50:14,678
It would be wise, my friend.

637
00:50:15,137 --> 00:50:16,597
Tell me...

638
00:50:16,764 --> 00:50:17,848
...friend...

639
00:50:18,849 --> 00:50:23,395
...when did Saruman the Wise
abandon reason for madness?

640
00:50:39,713 --> 00:50:46,888
{\an8}[CHORUS IN BLACK SPEECH]:
<i>One Ring for the Dark lord on his dark throne
<font color="#bd2600">(Ash Burz-Durbagu burzum-ishi)</font></i>

641
00:50:47,337 --> 00:51:00,267
{\an8}<i>In the Land of Mordor where the Shadows lie.
<font color="#bd2600">(Daghburz-ishi makha gulshu darulu.)</font></i>

642
00:51:00,518 --> 00:51:20,918
{\an8}<i>One Ring for the Dark lord on his dark throne
<font color="#bd2600">(Ash Burz-Durbagu burzum-ishi)</font></i>

643
00:51:02,893 --> 00:51:04,603
I gave you the chance...

644
00:51:05,729 --> 00:51:08,399
...of aiding me willingly...

645
00:51:08,566 --> 00:51:12,736
...but you have elected
the way of pain!

646
00:51:36,010 --> 00:51:37,511
SAM:
Mr. Frodo?

647
00:51:38,137 --> 00:51:39,930
Frodo? Frodo!

648
00:51:41,348 --> 00:51:44,602
-I thought I'd lost you.
-What are you talking about?

649
00:51:44,768 --> 00:51:47,771
-It's just something Gandalf said.
-What did he say?

650
00:51:48,606 --> 00:51:52,484
"Don't you lose him, Samwise Gamgee."
And I don't mean to.

651
00:51:52,735 --> 00:51:56,363
Sam, we're still in the Shire.
What could possibly happen?

652
00:51:59,325 --> 00:52:00,367
Frodo.

653
00:52:00,618 --> 00:52:02,870
-Merry, it's Frodo Baggins.
-Hello, Frodo.

654
00:52:03,037 --> 00:52:04,455
Get off him.

655
00:52:04,955 --> 00:52:06,457
Come on, Frodo.

656
00:52:06,624 --> 00:52:08,500
FRODO:
What's the meaning of this?

657
00:52:08,959 --> 00:52:10,711
You've been into Farmer Maggot's crop!

658
00:52:10,961 --> 00:52:12,129
[DOG BARKS]

659
00:52:13,213 --> 00:52:15,341
MAGGOT:
You get back here!

660
00:52:16,342 --> 00:52:17,676
Get out of my field!

661
00:52:17,843 --> 00:52:20,679
You'll know the devil
if I catch up with you!

662
00:52:20,888 --> 00:52:23,849
MERRY: I don't know why he's so upset.
It's only a couple of carrots.

663
00:52:24,016 --> 00:52:25,142
PIPPIN:
And some cabbages.

664
00:52:25,309 --> 00:52:28,228
And those three bags of potatoes
that we lifted last week.

665
00:52:28,395 --> 00:52:32,483
-And then the mushrooms the week before.
MERRY: Yes, Pippin. My point is...

666
00:52:32,691 --> 00:52:34,860
...he's clearly overreacting.

667
00:52:35,069 --> 00:52:36,570
Run!

668
00:52:50,042 --> 00:52:52,586
Oh, that was close.

669
00:52:53,671 --> 00:52:56,799
I think I've broken something.

670
00:52:57,800 --> 00:53:00,177
Trust a Brandybuck and a Took!

671
00:53:00,344 --> 00:53:04,014
What? That was just a detour.
A short cut.

672
00:53:04,181 --> 00:53:06,433
-Short cut to what?
-Mushrooms!

673
00:53:15,192 --> 00:53:16,694
PIPPIN:
That's mine.

674
00:53:19,446 --> 00:53:21,073
That's nice, Merry.

675
00:53:21,615 --> 00:53:23,617
MERRY:
Here's a nice one, Sam.

676
00:53:23,826 --> 00:53:26,370
I think we should get off the road.

677
00:53:27,955 --> 00:53:31,625
[SCREECHING]

678
00:53:35,546 --> 00:53:36,922
Get off the road!

679
00:53:37,131 --> 00:53:38,632
Quick!

680
00:53:46,974 --> 00:53:51,061
[HOOVES CLOPPING]

681
00:53:51,311 --> 00:53:52,813
Be quiet!

682
00:54:19,923 --> 00:54:21,675
[SNIFFS]

683
00:54:43,338 --> 00:54:45,362
THE RING [IN BLACK SPEECH]: <i> Lord...
<font color="#bd2600">(Durbgu...)</font></i>

684
00:54:59,129 --> 00:55:01,298
What was that?

685
00:55:20,567 --> 00:55:22,694
[SCREECHES]

686
00:55:33,997 --> 00:55:35,499
SAM:
Anything?

687
00:55:36,166 --> 00:55:37,668
Nothing.

688
00:55:38,377 --> 00:55:40,671
What is going on?

689
00:55:41,213 --> 00:55:45,008
That Black Rider was looking
for something. Or someone.

690
00:55:46,343 --> 00:55:47,845
Frodo?

691
00:55:48,554 --> 00:55:49,596
Get down!

692
00:56:06,530 --> 00:56:08,782
I have to leave the Shire.

693
00:56:09,783 --> 00:56:12,077
Sam and I must get to Bree.

694
00:56:12,286 --> 00:56:13,704
Right.

695
00:56:15,080 --> 00:56:17,374
Bucklebury Ferry. Follow me.

696
00:56:25,632 --> 00:56:27,009
PIPPIN:
Run!

697
00:56:28,218 --> 00:56:30,220
MERRY:
This way! Follow me!

698
00:56:33,765 --> 00:56:34,808
PIPPIN:
Run!

699
00:56:48,071 --> 00:56:49,823
MERRY:
Get the rope, Sam!

700
00:56:52,492 --> 00:56:54,036
Frodo!

701
00:56:54,745 --> 00:56:56,163
PIPPIN:
Run, Frodo!

702
00:56:56,496 --> 00:56:57,581
FRODO: Go!
PIPPIN: Hurry!

703
00:56:57,789 --> 00:57:00,417
MERRY:
Frodo, come on!

704
00:57:01,335 --> 00:57:03,337
SAM: Come on! Faster!
PIPPIN: Jump!

705
00:57:10,302 --> 00:57:11,803
[SCREECHES]

706
00:57:18,310 --> 00:57:22,522
-How far to the nearest crossing?
-The Brandywine Bridge. 20 miles.

707
00:57:37,120 --> 00:57:38,622
Come on.

708
00:57:49,800 --> 00:57:53,220
-What do you want?
-We're heading for the Prancing Pony.

709
00:57:56,723 --> 00:57:59,559
Hobbits. Four Hobbits!

710
00:57:59,726 --> 00:58:03,689
What's more, out of the Shire by your
talk. What business brings you to Bree?

711
00:58:04,106 --> 00:58:07,234
We wish to stay at the inn.
Our business is our own.

712
00:58:08,235 --> 00:58:10,821
All right, young sir.
I meant no offense.

713
00:58:10,988 --> 00:58:13,532
It's my job to ask questions
after nightfall.

714
00:58:13,699 --> 00:58:16,535
There's talk of strange folk abroad.

715
00:58:16,702 --> 00:58:18,870
Can't be too careful.

716
00:58:38,598 --> 00:58:42,102
Out of the way!
Watch where you're walking.

717
00:58:49,443 --> 00:58:52,154
[LAUGHING]

718
00:59:06,251 --> 00:59:07,878
Excuse me.

719
00:59:08,879 --> 00:59:11,715
Good evening, little masters.
What can I do for you?

720
00:59:11,882 --> 00:59:17,971
If you're seeking accommodation, we got
some cozy Hobbit-sized rooms available.

721
00:59:18,180 --> 00:59:22,809
Always proud to cater
to the Little Folk, Mister...?

722
00:59:23,977 --> 00:59:26,021
Underhill. My name's Underhill.

723
00:59:27,314 --> 00:59:29,816
-Underhill, yes.
-We're friends of Gandalf the Grey.

724
00:59:29,983 --> 00:59:33,153
-Can you tell him we've arrived?
-Gandalf?

725
00:59:33,570 --> 00:59:35,322
Gandalf.

726
00:59:36,156 --> 00:59:37,824
Oh, yes...

727
00:59:38,033 --> 00:59:40,160
...I remember. Elderly chap.

728
00:59:40,494 --> 00:59:43,413
Big grey beard, pointy hat.

729
00:59:43,830 --> 00:59:45,665
Not seen him for six months.

730
00:59:52,422 --> 00:59:53,715
What do we do now?

731
01:00:00,931 --> 01:00:02,182
Sam...

732
01:00:02,349 --> 01:00:04,226
...he'll be here. He'll come.

733
01:00:07,020 --> 01:00:09,064
MAN:
Get out of my way!

734
01:00:11,441 --> 01:00:13,110
What's that?

735
01:00:13,360 --> 01:00:15,862
This, my friend, is a pint.

736
01:00:16,029 --> 01:00:17,697
It comes in pints?

737
01:00:18,031 --> 01:00:21,743
-I'm getting one.
-You got a whole half already!

738
01:00:28,083 --> 01:00:31,920
That fellow's done nothing
but stare at you since we arrived.

739
01:00:35,465 --> 01:00:36,967
Excuse me.

740
01:00:38,760 --> 01:00:41,763
That Man in the corner. Who is he?

741
01:00:42,931 --> 01:00:47,352
He's one of them Rangers. They're
dangerous folk, wandering the Wilds.

742
01:00:47,602 --> 01:00:52,107
What his right name is, I've never heard,
but around here he's known as Strider.

743
01:00:54,484 --> 01:00:55,735
Strider.

744
01:01:08,748 --> 01:01:11,960
VOICE OF THE RING:
<i>Baggins.</i>

745
01:01:14,796 --> 01:01:16,965
<i>Baggins.</i>

746
01:01:22,345 --> 01:01:27,475
<i>Baggins. Baggins.</i>

747
01:01:29,311 --> 01:01:31,605
PIPPIN:
Baggins? Sure, I know a Baggins.

748
01:01:32,397 --> 01:01:35,275
He's over there. Frodo Baggins.

749
01:01:35,442 --> 01:01:38,486
He's my second cousin,
once removed on his mother's side...

750
01:01:38,653 --> 01:01:40,947
...and my third cousin, twice removed...

751
01:01:45,452 --> 01:01:47,204
-Pippin!
-Steady on, Frodo.

752
01:02:16,733 --> 01:02:19,194
SAURON:
You cannot hide.

753
01:02:22,155 --> 01:02:24,603
I see you.

754
01:02:24,628 --> 01:02:26,969
[IN BLACK SPEECH] I smell your blood.
<font color="#bd2600">(Nubin sherkuk.)</font>

755
01:02:26,993 --> 01:02:29,704
There is no life...

756
01:02:29,871 --> 01:02:32,082
...in the void.

757
01:02:32,249 --> 01:02:33,388
Only...

758
01:02:33,413 --> 01:02:34,644
[IN BLACK SPEECH] ...your blood.
<font color="#bd2600">(...sherkuk.)</font>

759
01:02:34,668 --> 01:02:36,169
...death.

760
01:02:42,175 --> 01:02:47,055
You draw far too much attention
to yourself, "Mr. Underhill."

761
01:02:51,726 --> 01:02:52,769
What do you want?

762
01:02:52,978 --> 01:02:55,021
A little more caution from you.
That is no trinket you carry.

763
01:02:55,397 --> 01:02:58,400
-I carry nothing.
-Indeed.

764
01:02:58,692 --> 01:03:01,236
I can avoid being seen if I wish...

765
01:03:01,403 --> 01:03:05,115
...but to disappear entirely,
that is a rare gift.

766
01:03:05,615 --> 01:03:08,243
-Who are you?
-Are you frightened?

767
01:03:09,494 --> 01:03:10,537
Yes.

768
01:03:10,704 --> 01:03:14,624
Not nearly frightened enough.
I know what hunts you.

769
01:03:16,418 --> 01:03:17,877
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

770
01:03:18,628 --> 01:03:21,172
Let him go!
Or I'll have you, Longshanks.

771
01:03:22,841 --> 01:03:26,970
You have a stout heart, little Hobbit.
But that will not save you.

772
01:03:27,137 --> 01:03:30,056
You can no longer wait
for the wizard, Frodo.

773
01:03:30,223 --> 01:03:31,224
They're coming.

774
01:03:31,558 --> 01:03:34,394
[HORSE GRUNTS]

775
01:03:36,741 --> 01:03:40,605
{\an8}[CHORUS IN ADÛNAIC]: <i> The Lords of Unending Life.
<font color="#bdaa00">(Bârî’n Katharâd)</font></i>

776
01:03:41,980 --> 01:03:47,180
{\an8}<i>Behold! The Nine!
<font color="#bdaa00">(Îdô! Nidir!)</font></i>

777
01:03:47,383 --> 01:03:51,399
{\an8}<i>We are... we take
<font color="#bdaa00">(Nênâkham... nêpâm)</font></i>

778
01:03:52,785 --> 01:03:57,505
{\an8}<i>the power and glory
<font color="#bdaa00">([a]bârat-aglar)</font></i>

779
01:04:41,378 --> 01:04:43,630
[SCREECHING]

780
01:04:54,933 --> 01:04:56,434
What are they?

781
01:04:58,603 --> 01:05:00,730
They were once Men.

782
01:05:01,231 --> 01:05:03,441
Great kings of Men.

783
01:05:03,650 --> 01:05:06,820
Then Sauron the Deceiver gave to them
nine rings of power.

784
01:05:07,404 --> 01:05:10,490
Blinded by their greed,
they took them without question.

785
01:05:10,740 --> 01:05:14,077
One by one, falling into darkness.

786
01:05:14,244 --> 01:05:16,746
Now they are slaves to his will.

787
01:05:19,124 --> 01:05:20,834
They are the Nazgûl.

788
01:05:21,000 --> 01:05:23,753
Ringwraiths. Neither living nor dead.

789
01:05:24,504 --> 01:05:25,964
At all times they feel...

790
01:05:26,131 --> 01:05:28,091
<i>...the presence of the Ring...</i>

791
01:05:28,258 --> 01:05:32,804
<i>...drawn to the power of the One.
They will never stop hunting you.</i>

792
01:05:42,772 --> 01:05:45,692
FRODO: Where are you taking us?
-Into the Wild.

793
01:05:53,867 --> 01:05:57,996
How do we know this Strider
is a friend of Gandalf?

794
01:05:58,163 --> 01:06:00,999
I think a servant of the enemy
would look fairer...

795
01:06:01,374 --> 01:06:05,295
-...and feel fouler.
-He's foul enough.

796
01:06:05,879 --> 01:06:08,715
We have no choice but to trust him.

797
01:06:08,882 --> 01:06:12,343
-But where is he leading us?
STRIDER: To Rivendell, Master Gamgee.

798
01:06:14,721 --> 01:06:18,016
-To the house of Elrond.
SAM: Did you hear that? Rivendell.

799
01:06:18,558 --> 01:06:21,352
We're going to see the Elves.

800
01:06:38,620 --> 01:06:40,246
[HOBBITS WHISPERING]

801
01:06:42,999 --> 01:06:47,253
-Gentlemen, we do not stop till nightfall.
-What about breakfast?

802
01:06:47,420 --> 01:06:50,089
-You've already had it.
-We've had one, yes.

803
01:06:50,256 --> 01:06:52,509
What about second breakfast?

804
01:06:55,929 --> 01:06:59,098
Don't think he knows
about second breakfast, Pip.

805
01:06:59,265 --> 01:07:04,521
What about elevenses? Luncheon?
Afternoon tea? Dinner? Supper?

806
01:07:04,729 --> 01:07:08,900
-He knows about them, doesn't he?
-I wouldn't count on it.

807
01:07:14,364 --> 01:07:15,949
MERRY:
Pippin!

808
01:07:32,465 --> 01:07:35,969
What do they eat
when they can't get Hobbit?

809
01:07:51,612 --> 01:07:54,297
STRIDER [SINGS IN SINDARIN]: <i> Tinúviel the elven-fair,
<font color="#00bd00">(Tinúviel elvanui,)</font></i>

810
01:07:55,869 --> 01:07:59,325
<i>Immortal maiden...
<font color="#00bd00">(Elleth alfirin...)</font></i>

811
01:08:00,193 --> 01:08:02,112
<i>...elven-wise
<font color="#00bd00">(...edhelhael)</font></i>

812
01:08:03,788 --> 01:08:10,572
<i>About him cast her night-dark hair
<font color="#00bd00">(O hon ring finnil fuinui)</font></i>

813
01:08:11,673 --> 01:08:14,607
<i>And arms like silver...
<font color="#00bd00">(A renc gelebrin...)</font></i>

814
01:08:14,632 --> 01:08:16,843
Who is she?

815
01:08:17,510 --> 01:08:20,138
This woman you sing of.

816
01:08:23,516 --> 01:08:25,977
'Tis the lady of Lúthien.

817
01:08:26,144 --> 01:08:31,316
The Elf-maiden who gave her love
to Beren, a mortal.

818
01:08:33,151 --> 01:08:35,278
What happened to her?

819
01:08:37,488 --> 01:08:39,991
She died.

820
01:08:44,037 --> 01:08:46,372
Get some sleep, Frodo.

821
01:08:56,633 --> 01:09:00,720
SARUMAN: <i> The power of Isengard
is at your command...</i>

822
01:09:00,887 --> 01:09:05,350
<i>...Sauron, Lord of the Earth.</i>

823
01:09:05,617 --> 01:09:08,353
[VOICES WHISPERING IN BLACK SPEECH]

824
01:09:08,686 --> 01:09:14,484
SAURON:
<i>Build me an army worthy of Mordor.</i>

825
01:09:20,198 --> 01:09:24,661
What orders from Mordor, my lord?
What does the Eye command?

826
01:09:25,078 --> 01:09:27,038
We have work to do.

827
01:10:09,622 --> 01:10:14,252
The trees are strong, my lord.
Their roots go deep.

828
01:10:14,627 --> 01:10:16,462
Rip them all down.

829
01:10:43,906 --> 01:10:46,784
This was the great watchtower
of Amon Sûl.

830
01:10:48,494 --> 01:10:51,164
We shall rest here tonight.

831
01:11:02,884 --> 01:11:06,304
These are for you.
Keep them close.

832
01:11:06,512 --> 01:11:09,015
I'm going to have a look around.

833
01:11:11,392 --> 01:11:13,311
Stay here.

834
01:11:15,855 --> 01:11:18,024
MERRY:
My tomato's burst.

835
01:11:18,274 --> 01:11:20,151
PIPPIN:
Could I have some bacon?

836
01:11:20,359 --> 01:11:22,320
MERRY:
Want a tomato, Sam?

837
01:11:22,695 --> 01:11:26,365
-What are you doing?!
-Tomatoes, sausages, nice crispy bacon.

838
01:11:26,532 --> 01:11:29,285
SAM: We saved some for you, Mr. Frodo.
FRODO: Put it out, you fools!

839
01:11:29,494 --> 01:11:33,498
-Put it out!
PIPPIN: That's nice! Ash on my tomatoes!

840
01:11:34,040 --> 01:11:36,167
[RINGWRAITHS SCREECHING]

841
01:11:41,923 --> 01:11:43,674
Go!

842
01:12:07,876 --> 01:12:11,925
{\an8}[CHORUS IN ADÛNAIC]: <i> The Lords of Unending Life.
<font color="#bdaa00">(Bârî’n Katharâd.)</font></i>

843
01:12:13,278 --> 01:12:17,116
{\an8}<i>Behold! We, the Nine.
<font color="#bdaa00">(Îdô! Nidir, nê.)</font></i>

844
01:12:18,806 --> 01:12:24,204
{\an8}<i>We take unto ourselves the power.
<font color="#bdaa00">(Nêpâm nêd abârat.)</font></i>

845
01:12:25,610 --> 01:12:29,751
{\an8}<i>We are the Nine.
<font color="#bdaa00">(Dir nênâkham.)</font></i>

846
01:12:31,089 --> 01:12:41,543
{\an8}<i>We renounce our Maker.
<font color="#bdaa00">(Nêbâbîtham Magânanê.)</font></i>

847
01:12:37,103 --> 01:12:38,563
Back, you devils!

848
01:12:41,996 --> 01:12:48,014
{\an8}<i>We cleave the darkness.
<font color="#bdaa00">(Nêtabdam dâur.)</font></i>

849
01:12:49,031 --> 01:12:50,913
VOICE OF THE RING [IN BLACK SPEECH]: <i> In the void...
<font color="#bd2600">(Gûm-ishi...)</font></i>

850
01:12:53,014 --> 01:12:54,286
<i>Only...
<font color="#bd2600">(Ashi...)</font></i>

851
01:13:13,835 --> 01:13:15,336
<i>Death...
<font color="#bd2600">(Gurum...)</font></i>

852
01:13:30,516 --> 01:13:33,528
VOICE OF THE RING: <i> Where the Shadows lie...
<font color="#bd2600">(Makha Gulshu darulu...)</font></i>

853
01:13:33,808 --> 01:13:39,378
<i>In the Land of Mordor where Shadows lie.
<font color="#bd2600">(Daghburz-ishi makha Gulshu darulu.)</font></i>

854
01:13:39,635 --> 01:13:41,959
[VOICE OF THE RING HISSES]

855
01:14:02,063 --> 01:14:03,314
Frodo!

856
01:14:07,360 --> 01:14:09,195
-Frodo.
-Oh, Sam.

857
01:14:46,232 --> 01:14:47,233
Strider!

858
01:14:50,027 --> 01:14:55,533
-Help him, Strider.
-He's been stabbed by a Morgul blade.

859
01:14:57,034 --> 01:15:01,914
This is beyond my skill to heal.
He needs Elvish medicine.

860
01:15:06,502 --> 01:15:07,545
Hurry!

861
01:15:07,753 --> 01:15:11,716
We're six days from Rivendell!
He'll never make it!

862
01:15:11,924 --> 01:15:13,759
Hold on, Frodo.

863
01:15:15,344 --> 01:15:16,387
Gandalf!

864
01:15:33,279 --> 01:15:36,407
[METAL CLANKING]

865
01:15:46,125 --> 01:15:52,864
{\an8}[SINGING IN QUENYA]: <i> The earth...
<font color="#0078bd">(I ce...)</font></i>

866
01:15:52,889 --> 01:16:03,508
{\an8}<i>The earth groans...
<font color="#0078bd">(I cemen nurrua...)</font></i>

867
01:16:03,774 --> 01:16:11,257
{\an8}<i>and the wind...
<font color="#0078bd">(ar i súre...)</font></i>

868
01:16:11,281 --> 01:16:16,736
{\an8}<i>the wind...
<font color="#0078bd">(i súre...)</font></i>

869
01:16:13,917 --> 01:16:20,793
[WHISPERS INSTRUCTIONS TO THE MOTH]

870
01:16:17,148 --> 01:16:24,455
{\an8}<i>is crying!
<font color="#0078bd">(naina!)</font></i>

871
01:17:09,750 --> 01:17:11,043
[GROWLS]

872
01:17:54,295 --> 01:17:57,381
Look, Frodo. It's Mr. Bilbo's trolls.

873
01:17:59,550 --> 01:18:02,386
Mr. Frodo? He's going cold.

874
01:18:05,347 --> 01:18:07,099
Is he going to die?

875
01:18:07,308 --> 01:18:12,188
He's passing into the Shadow World.
He'll soon become a Wraith like them.

876
01:18:12,438 --> 01:18:14,023
[RINGWRAITHS SCREECHING]

877
01:18:17,359 --> 01:18:21,197
-They're close.
-Sam, do you know the Athelas plant?

878
01:18:21,363 --> 01:18:22,865
-Athelas?
-Kingsfoil.

879
01:18:23,032 --> 01:18:24,116
Kingsfoil, aye, it's a weed.

880
01:18:24,325 --> 01:18:27,453
It may help to slow the poisoning.
Hurry!

881
01:18:41,842 --> 01:18:45,971
WOMAN: What's this?
A Ranger caught off his guard?

882
01:18:50,403 --> 01:19:14,853
{\an8}[CHORUS SINGS IN SINDARIN]: <i> Tinúviel the elven-fair,
<font color="#00bd00">(Tinúviel elvanui,)</font></i>

883
01:19:10,871 --> 01:19:11,914
Frodo.

884
01:19:13,874 --> 01:19:17,100
[IN SINDARIN] <font color="#00bd00">(Im Arwen - telin le thaed.)</font>

885
01:19:14,856 --> 01:19:28,720
{\an8}<i>Immortal maiden...,
<font color="#00bd00">(Elleth alfirin e...)</font></i>

886
01:19:19,434 --> 01:19:21,301
<font color="#00bd00">(Lasto beth nîn...)</font>

887
01:19:21,519 --> 01:19:23,685
<font color="#00bd00">(Tolo dan nan galad.)</font>

888
01:19:28,847 --> 01:19:30,683
Who is she?

889
01:19:31,350 --> 01:19:33,102
Frodo.

890
01:19:33,352 --> 01:19:36,855
-She's an Elf.
-He's fading.

891
01:19:39,108 --> 01:19:41,277
[IN WESTRON]
He's not going to last.

892
01:19:41,485 --> 01:19:44,154
We must get him to my father.

893
01:19:44,905 --> 01:19:47,783
-I've been looking for you for two days.
-Where are you taking him?

894
01:19:47,950 --> 01:19:54,039
There are five Wraiths behind you.
Where the other four are, I do not know.

895
01:19:55,132 --> 01:19:57,675
[IN SINDARIN] <font color="#00bd00">(Dartho guin Beriain - rych le ad tolthathon.)</font>

896
01:19:57,700 --> 01:19:59,508
<font color="#00bd00">(Hon mabathon - rochon ellint im.)</font>

897
01:20:00,313 --> 01:20:01,718
<font color="#00bd00">(Andelu i ven.)</font>

898
01:20:01,880 --> 01:20:03,132
What are they saying?

899
01:20:03,350 --> 01:20:05,479
ARWEN: [Frodo is dying.] <font color="#00bd00">(Frodo fîr. Ae athradon i hîr...)</font>

900
01:20:05,519 --> 01:20:08,230
<font color="#00bd00">(...tûr gwaith nîn beriatha hon.)</font>

901
01:20:09,221 --> 01:20:10,889
[IN WESTRON]
I do not fear them.

902
01:20:14,685 --> 01:20:16,645
[IN SINDARIN] As you wish.
<font color="#00bd00">(Be iest lîn.)</font>

903
01:20:20,733 --> 01:20:22,151
[IN WESTRON]
Arwen...

904
01:20:22,318 --> 01:20:24,682
...ride hard. Don't look back.

905
01:20:24,706 --> 01:20:26,913
[IN SINDARIN] Ride fast, Asfaloth, ride fast!
<font color="#00bd00">(Noro lim, Asfaloth, noro lim!)</font>

906
01:20:30,576 --> 01:20:34,955
What are you doing?!
Those Wraiths are still out there!

907
01:21:36,795 --> 01:21:40,975
{\an8}[CHORUS IN ADÛNAIC]: <i> The Lords of Unending Life.
<font color="#bdaa00">(Bârî’n Katharâd.)</font></i>

908
01:21:41,814 --> 01:21:42,981
[SCREECHES]

909
01:21:42,270 --> 01:21:47,725
{\an8}<i>Behold! We are... we take
<font color="#bdaa00">(Îdô! Kham... nêpâm)</font></i>

910
01:21:45,109 --> 01:21:47,653
Ride fast, Asfaloth!
<font color="#00bd00">(Noro lim, Asfaloth!)</font>

911
01:21:47,747 --> 01:21:51,433
{\an8}<i>We take unto ourselves
<font color="#bdaa00">(Nênâkham nêpâm)</font></i>

912
01:21:52,663 --> 01:21:57,963
{\an8}<i>the power and glory
<font color="#bdaa00">([a]bârat-aglar)</font></i>

913
01:21:57,988 --> 01:22:01,498
{\an8}<i>The Lords of Unending Life
<font color="#bdaa00">(Nêbâ Katharâd)</font></i>

914
01:22:02,846 --> 01:22:07,996
{\an8}<i>We are the Nine
<font color="#bdaa00">(Nidir nênâ)</font></i>

915
01:22:08,021 --> 01:22:16,321
{\an8}<i>We renounce the darkness
<font color="#bdaa00">(Nêbîtham [dâ]ur)</font></i>

916
01:22:29,570 --> 01:22:32,281
Give up the halfling, She-Elf.

917
01:22:33,198 --> 01:22:35,784
[IN WESTRON]
If you want him, come and claim him.

918
01:22:47,838 --> 01:22:50,176
[IN SINDARIN] Waters of the Misty Mountains, listen to the great word;
<font color="#00bd00">(Nîn o Chithaeglir, lasto beth daer;)</font>

919
01:22:50,568 --> 01:22:53,515
flow waters of Loudwater, against the Ringwraiths!
<font color="#00bd00">(rimmo nîn Bruinen, dan in Ulaer!)</font>

920
01:22:53,706 --> 01:22:56,325
Waters of the Misty Mountains, listen to the great word;
<font color="#00bd00">(Nîn o Chithaeglir, lasto beth daer;)</font>

921
01:22:56,873 --> 01:22:59,922
flow waters of Loudwater, against the Ringwraiths!
<font color="#00bd00">(rimmo nîn Bruinen, dan in Ulaer!)</font>

922
01:23:29,671 --> 01:23:32,174
[IN WESTRON]
No. No!

923
01:23:35,427 --> 01:23:37,721
Frodo, no.

924
01:23:37,930 --> 01:23:40,224
Frodo, don't give in.

925
01:23:40,432 --> 01:23:42,434
Not now.

926
01:23:53,362 --> 01:23:55,864
ARWEN:
<i>What grace is given me...</i>

927
01:23:56,532 --> 01:23:58,367
<i>...let it pass to him.</i>

928
01:23:58,617 --> 01:24:00,744
<i>Let him be spared.</i>

929
01:24:01,374 --> 01:24:03,417
<i>Save him.</i>

930
01:24:05,596 --> 01:24:10,009
[IN SINDARIN] Hear my voice. Come back to the light.
<font color="#00bd00">(Lasto beth nîn. Tolo dan nan galad.)</font>

931
01:24:15,801 --> 01:24:20,973
-Where am I?
GANDALF: You are in the house of Elrond.

932
01:24:21,431 --> 01:24:27,938
And it is 10:00 in the morning
on October 24th, if you want to know.

933
01:24:29,898 --> 01:24:33,694
-Gandalf!
-Yes, I'm here.

934
01:24:35,320 --> 01:24:38,407
And you're lucky to be here too.

935
01:24:39,074 --> 01:24:43,078
A few more hours and you
would have been beyond our aid.

936
01:24:43,287 --> 01:24:47,416
But you have some strength in you,
my dear Hobbit.

937
01:24:55,007 --> 01:24:57,509
What happened, Gandalf?

938
01:24:58,468 --> 01:25:03,849
-Why didn't you meet us?
-I am sorry, Frodo.

939
01:25:08,604 --> 01:25:10,355
I was delayed.

940
01:25:11,231 --> 01:25:15,444
A friendship with Saruman
is not lightly thrown aside.

941
01:25:19,531 --> 01:25:24,202
One ill turn deserves another.
It is over.

942
01:25:24,494 --> 01:25:27,247
Embrace the power of the Ring...

943
01:25:27,789 --> 01:25:30,334
...or embrace your own destruction!

944
01:25:32,628 --> 01:25:36,506
GANDALF:
There is only one Lord of the Ring.

945
01:25:36,757 --> 01:25:40,761
Only one who can bend it to his will.

946
01:25:41,553 --> 01:25:45,515
And he does not share power.

947
01:25:45,766 --> 01:25:48,518
[BIRD SCREECHES]

948
01:25:59,863 --> 01:26:03,241
So you have chosen death.

949
01:26:13,293 --> 01:26:17,089
Gandalf? What is it?

950
01:26:18,048 --> 01:26:19,841
Nothing, Frodo.

951
01:26:20,509 --> 01:26:22,344
SAM:
Frodo!

952
01:26:22,552 --> 01:26:23,595
Frodo!

953
01:26:23,804 --> 01:26:26,181
-Sam.
-Bless you, you're awake!

954
01:26:26,390 --> 01:26:29,101
Sam has hardly left your side.

955
01:26:29,351 --> 01:26:31,520
We were that worried about you.
Weren't we, Mr. Gandalf?

956
01:26:31,895 --> 01:26:37,025
By the skills of Lord Elrond,
you're beginning to mend.

957
01:26:38,527 --> 01:26:42,114
Welcome to Rivendell, Frodo Baggins.

958
01:27:30,162 --> 01:27:33,498
FRODO: Bilbo!
-Hello, Frodo, my lad.

959
01:27:33,665 --> 01:27:35,375
Bilbo.

960
01:27:40,380 --> 01:27:42,132
FRODO:
<i>"There and Back Again:</i>

961
01:27:42,382 --> 01:27:45,135
<i>A Hobbit's Tale</i>, by Bilbo Baggins."

962
01:27:48,180 --> 01:27:51,767
-This is wonderful.
-I meant to go back...

963
01:27:52,100 --> 01:27:55,896
...wonder at the powers of Mirkwood...

964
01:27:56,354 --> 01:27:58,648
...visit Lake-town...

965
01:27:58,899 --> 01:28:02,277
...see the Lonely Mountain again.

966
01:28:02,694 --> 01:28:07,616
But age, it seems,
has finally caught up with me.

967
01:28:19,711 --> 01:28:21,505
FRODO:
I miss the Shire.

968
01:28:21,922 --> 01:28:27,052
I spent all my childhood pretending
I was off somewhere else.

969
01:28:27,385 --> 01:28:30,972
Off with you,
on one of your adventures.

970
01:28:33,934 --> 01:28:37,521
But my own adventure turned out
to be quite different.

971
01:28:42,734 --> 01:28:45,946
I'm not like you, Bilbo.

972
01:28:47,072 --> 01:28:49,407
My dear boy.

973
01:28:53,495 --> 01:28:57,457
SAM: Now, what have I forgotten?
-Packed already?

974
01:28:58,250 --> 01:29:00,043
No harm in being prepared.

975
01:29:00,252 --> 01:29:02,838
-I thought you wanted to see the Elves.
-I do.

976
01:29:03,004 --> 01:29:05,924
-More than anything.
-I did.

977
01:29:06,091 --> 01:29:08,009
It's just...

978
01:29:08,760 --> 01:29:11,429
We did what Gandalf wanted, didn't we?

979
01:29:11,596 --> 01:29:15,267
We got the Ring this far,
to Rivendell. And I thought...

980
01:29:15,475 --> 01:29:18,770
...seeing as how you're on the mend,
we'd be off soon.

981
01:29:18,979 --> 01:29:20,689
Off home.

982
01:29:24,860 --> 01:29:26,862
You are right, Sam.

983
01:29:29,030 --> 01:29:31,783
We did what we set out to do.

984
01:29:32,367 --> 01:29:34,953
The Ring will be safe in Rivendell.

985
01:29:39,040 --> 01:29:41,376
I am ready to go home.

986
01:29:42,127 --> 01:29:44,212
ELROND:
His strength returns.

987
01:29:44,379 --> 01:29:50,093
That wound will never fully heal.
He will carry it the rest of his life.

988
01:29:50,635 --> 01:29:53,221
And yet to have come so far
still bearing the Ring...

989
01:29:53,388 --> 01:29:57,100
...the Hobbit has shown extraordinary
resilience to its evil.

990
01:29:57,309 --> 01:30:00,645
It is a burden he should never
have had to bear.

991
01:30:00,896 --> 01:30:06,318
-We can ask no more of Frodo.
-Gandalf, the enemy is moving.

992
01:30:06,526 --> 01:30:11,156
Sauron's forces are massing in the East.
His Eye is fixed on Rivendell.

993
01:30:11,406 --> 01:30:14,159
And Saruman, you tell me, has betrayed us.

994
01:30:14,326 --> 01:30:17,579
Our list of allies grows thin.

995
01:30:18,330 --> 01:30:21,124
His treachery runs deeper
than you know.

996
01:30:21,333 --> 01:30:25,003
By foul craft, Saruman
has crossed Orcs with Goblin-men.

997
01:30:25,170 --> 01:30:27,631
He's breeding an army
in the caverns of Isengard.

998
01:30:27,923 --> 01:30:32,510
An army that can move in sunlight
and cover great distance at speed.

999
01:30:32,677 --> 01:30:35,096
Saruman is coming for the Ring.

1000
01:30:35,555 --> 01:30:39,601
This evil cannot be concealed
by the power of the Elves.

1001
01:30:39,809 --> 01:30:44,189
We do not have the strength
to fight both Mordor and Isengard!

1002
01:30:48,026 --> 01:30:49,110
Gandalf...

1003
01:30:50,445 --> 01:30:53,031
...the Ring cannot stay here.

1004
01:31:12,550 --> 01:31:15,720
ELROND: <i> This peril belongs
to all Middle-earth.</i>

1005
01:31:15,971 --> 01:31:18,682
<i>They must decide now how to end it.</i>

1006
01:31:19,724 --> 01:31:23,311
The time of the Elves is over.
My people are leaving these shores.

1007
01:31:23,979 --> 01:31:27,565
Who will you look to when we've gone?
The Dwarves?

1008
01:31:27,732 --> 01:31:32,862
They hide in mountains seeking riches.
They care not for the troubles of others.

1009
01:31:34,489 --> 01:31:37,325
It is in Men
that we must place our hope.

1010
01:31:37,659 --> 01:31:39,369
Men?

1011
01:31:40,245 --> 01:31:43,498
Men are weak.
The race of Men is failing.

1012
01:31:43,665 --> 01:31:48,128
The blood of Númenor is all but spent,
its pride and dignity forgotten.

1013
01:31:48,420 --> 01:31:51,923
It is because of Men
the Ring survives.

1014
01:31:52,132 --> 01:31:53,758
I was there, Gandalf.

1015
01:31:54,426 --> 01:31:57,262
<i>I was there 3000 years ago...</i>

1016
01:32:04,102 --> 01:32:06,521
<i>...when Isildur took the Ring.</i>

1017
01:32:06,688 --> 01:32:10,608
I was there the day
the strength of Men failed.

1018
01:32:13,153 --> 01:32:15,697
Isildur, hurry! Follow me.

1019
01:32:17,282 --> 01:32:20,910
ELROND: <i> I led Isildur into the heart
of Mount Doom...</i>

1020
01:32:21,161 --> 01:32:24,706
<i>...where the Ring was forged,
the one place it could be destroyed.</i>

1021
01:32:24,873 --> 01:32:27,459
Cast it into the fire!

1022
01:32:27,792 --> 01:32:30,628
[VOICE OF THE RING
WHISPERS IN BLACK SPEECH]

1023
01:32:32,630 --> 01:32:36,426
-Destroy it!
-No.

1024
01:32:37,761 --> 01:32:39,929
Isildur!

1025
01:32:40,388 --> 01:32:45,143
ELROND: <i> It should have ended that day,
but evil was allowed to endure.</i>

1026
01:32:49,230 --> 01:32:53,485
Isildur kept the Ring.
The line of kings is broken.

1027
01:32:54,402 --> 01:32:58,073
There's no strength left
in the world of Men.

1028
01:32:58,239 --> 01:33:03,078
-They're scattered, divided, leaderless.
-There is one who could unite them.

1029
01:33:03,286 --> 01:33:06,664
One who could reclaim
the throne of Gondor.

1030
01:33:08,333 --> 01:33:12,170
He turned from that path
a long time ago.

1031
01:33:12,337 --> 01:33:14,464
He has chosen exile.

1032
01:33:45,703 --> 01:33:47,705
You are no Elf.

1033
01:33:47,872 --> 01:33:49,958
Men of the South are welcome here.

1034
01:33:50,542 --> 01:33:54,045
-Who are you?
-I am a friend to Gandalf the Grey.

1035
01:33:55,547 --> 01:33:58,383
Then we are here on common purpose...

1036
01:33:58,758 --> 01:34:00,218
...friend.

1037
01:34:15,400 --> 01:34:18,319
The shards of Narsil.

1038
01:34:21,781 --> 01:34:26,244
The blade that cut the Ring
from Sauron's hand.

1039
01:34:29,164 --> 01:34:31,416
It's still sharp.

1040
01:34:40,300 --> 01:34:43,386
But no more than a broken heirloom.

1041
01:35:10,205 --> 01:35:13,249
Why do you fear the past?

1042
01:35:14,125 --> 01:35:19,464
You are Isildur's heir,
not Isildur himself.

1043
01:35:19,714 --> 01:35:23,134
You are not bound to his fate.

1044
01:35:23,635 --> 01:35:27,639
The same blood flows in my veins.

1045
01:35:30,642 --> 01:35:33,228
The same weakness.

1046
01:35:35,939 --> 01:35:38,733
Your time will come.

1047
01:35:38,942 --> 01:35:43,321
You will face the same evil.
And you will defeat it.

1048
01:35:46,459 --> 01:35:48,921
[IN SINDARIN] <font color="#00bd00">(A si i-Dhúath ú-orthor, Aragorn.)</font>

1049
01:35:49,904 --> 01:35:53,506
<font color="#00bd00">(Ú or le... a ú or nin.)</font>

1050
01:36:04,850 --> 01:36:08,097
<font color="#00bd00">(Renich i lú i erui govannem?)</font>

1051
01:36:11,641 --> 01:36:16,187
<font color="#00bd00">(Nauthannen i ned ôl reniannen.)</font>

1052
01:36:16,716 --> 01:36:19,243
<font color="#00bd00">(Gwenwin in enninath.)</font>

1053
01:36:20,915 --> 01:36:24,315
<font color="#00bd00">(Ú-'arnech in naeth i si celich.)</font>

1054
01:36:25,752 --> 01:36:27,829
<font color="#00bd00">(Renich i beth i pennen?)</font>

1055
01:36:33,871 --> 01:36:36,541
[IN WESTRON]
You said you'd bind yourself to me...

1056
01:36:38,543 --> 01:36:43,548
...forsaking the immortal life
of your people.

1057
01:36:44,674 --> 01:36:46,551
[IN WESTRON]
And to that I hold.

1058
01:36:46,694 --> 01:36:50,322
I would rather share
one lifetime with you...

1059
01:36:50,596 --> 01:36:54,475
...than face all the Ages
of this world alone.

1060
01:37:03,234 --> 01:37:06,696
I choose a mortal life.

1061
01:37:08,031 --> 01:37:12,285
-You cannot give me this.
-It is mine to give to whom I will...

1062
01:37:15,538 --> 01:37:18,041
...like my heart.

1063
01:37:33,806 --> 01:37:37,518
ELROND: Strangers from distant lands,
friends of old...

1064
01:37:37,727 --> 01:37:41,647
...you've been summoned here
to answer the threat of Mordor.

1065
01:37:42,273 --> 01:37:47,153
Middle-earth stands upon the brink
of destruction. None can escape it.

1066
01:37:47,403 --> 01:37:50,907
You will unite, or you will fall.

1067
01:37:51,115 --> 01:37:55,411
Each race is bound to this fate,
this one doom.

1068
01:37:57,246 --> 01:38:00,750
Bring forth the Ring, Frodo.

1069
01:38:14,806 --> 01:38:16,557
So it is true.

1070
01:38:33,991 --> 01:38:36,119
In a dream...

1071
01:38:37,703 --> 01:38:40,832
...I saw the eastern sky grow dark...

1072
01:38:41,124 --> 01:38:42,834
...but in the West
a pale light lingered.

1073
01:38:43,626 --> 01:38:45,378
A voice was crying:

1074
01:38:45,670 --> 01:38:48,589
"Your doom is near at hand.

1075
01:38:49,590 --> 01:38:52,343
Isildur's Bane is found."

1076
01:38:54,563 --> 01:38:56,322
THE RING [IN BLACK SPEECH]: <i> In the cold...
<font color="#bd2600">(Kelkum-ishi...)</font></i>

1077
01:38:56,347 --> 01:38:58,182
Isildur's Bane.

1078
01:38:58,850 --> 01:38:59,482
Boromir!

1079
01:38:59,507 --> 01:39:01,940
[CHANTS IN BLACK SPEECH] One Ring to rule them all...
<font color="#bd2600">(Ash Nazg durbatulûk...)</font>

1080
01:39:00,665 --> 01:39:02,809
{\an8}[THE RING]: <i> Three Rings for the Elven-kings...
<font color="#bd2600">(Shre nazg golugranu...)</font></i>

1081
01:39:03,186 --> 01:39:06,695
...One Ring to find them...
<font color="#bd2600">(...Ash Nazg gimbatul...)</font>

1082
01:39:03,188 --> 01:39:06,495
{\an8}<i>I smell your blood.
<font color="#bd2600">(Nubin sherkuk.)</font></i>

1083
01:39:06,596 --> 01:39:08,295
{\an8}<i>Seven for the Dwarf-lords.
<font color="#bd2600">(Ombi kuzddurbagu.)</font></i>

1084
01:39:07,060 --> 01:39:09,823
...One Ring to bring them all...
<font color="#bd2600">(...Ash Nazg thrakatulûk...)</font>

1085
01:39:09,508 --> 01:39:11,289
{\an8}<i>I smell your blood.</i>
<i><font color="#bd2600">(Nubin sherkuk.)</font></i>

1086
01:39:11,314 --> 01:39:13,014
{\an8}<i>In the cold... One for the Dark Lord...
<font color="#bd2600">(Kelkum-ishi... Ash Burz-Durbagu...)</font></i>

1087
01:39:13,039 --> 01:39:15,284
...and in the darkness...
<font color="#bd2600">(...agh burzum-ishi...)</font>

1088
01:39:13,031 --> 01:39:15,274
{\an8}<i>...in the darkness...
<font color="#bd2600">(...burzum-ishi...)</font></i>

1089
01:39:15,309 --> 01:39:17,027
...bind them!
<font color="#bd2600">(...krimpatul!)</font>

1090
01:39:23,332 --> 01:39:27,170
Never before has any voice uttered the
words of that tongue here in Imladris.

1091
01:39:27,336 --> 01:39:31,048
[IN WESTRON] I do not ask your pardon,
Master Elrond...

1092
01:39:31,215 --> 01:39:33,342
...for the Black Speech of Mordor...

1093
01:39:33,634 --> 01:39:35,011
...may yet be heard...

1094
01:39:35,178 --> 01:39:38,181
...in every corner of the West!

1095
01:39:38,347 --> 01:39:41,017
The Ring is altogether evil.

1096
01:39:41,350 --> 01:39:42,852
It is a gift.

1097
01:39:43,436 --> 01:39:45,521
A gift to the foes of Mordor.

1098
01:39:46,147 --> 01:39:48,232
Why not use this Ring?

1099
01:39:48,441 --> 01:39:51,194
Long has my father,
the Steward of Gondor...

1100
01:39:51,402 --> 01:39:55,740
...kept the forces of Mordor at bay.
By the blood of our people...

1101
01:39:56,032 --> 01:39:58,242
...are your lands kept safe.

1102
01:40:00,036 --> 01:40:04,373
Give Gondor the weapon of the enemy.
Let us use it against him.

1103
01:40:04,665 --> 01:40:08,419
You cannot wield it.
None of us can.

1104
01:40:09,045 --> 01:40:13,090
The One Ring answers to Sauron alone.
It has no other master.

1105
01:40:13,257 --> 01:40:16,802
And what would a Ranger know
of this matter?

1106
01:40:17,094 --> 01:40:19,096
This is no mere Ranger.

1107
01:40:20,097 --> 01:40:23,768
He is Aragorn, son of Arathorn.

1108
01:40:24,268 --> 01:40:27,188
You owe him your allegiance.

1109
01:40:31,275 --> 01:40:33,194
Aragorn.

1110
01:40:34,946 --> 01:40:37,782
This is Isildur's heir?

1111
01:40:40,117 --> 01:40:42,828
And heir to the throne of Gondor.

1112
01:40:44,924 --> 01:40:46,422
[IN SINDARIN] <font color="#00bd00">(Havo dad, Legolas.)</font>

1113
01:40:49,794 --> 01:40:52,630
Gondor has no king.

1114
01:40:54,465 --> 01:40:56,133
Gondor needs no king.

1115
01:41:02,807 --> 01:41:06,477
Aragorn is right. We cannot use it.

1116
01:41:07,478 --> 01:41:10,982
You have only one choice.

1117
01:41:11,232 --> 01:41:13,609
The Ring must be destroyed.

1118
01:41:15,444 --> 01:41:18,531
[VOICE OF THE RING
WHISPERS IN BLACK SPEECH]

1119
01:41:18,823 --> 01:41:21,367
What are we waiting for?

1120
01:41:26,835 --> 01:41:29,955
{\an8}THE RING: <i> In the Land of Mordor where...
<font color="#bd2600">(Daghburz-ishi makha...)</font></i>

1121
01:41:30,308 --> 01:41:31,625
{\an8}<i>...your blood.
<font color="#bd2600">(...sherkuk.)</font></i>

1122
01:41:33,504 --> 01:41:36,507
The Ring cannot be destroyed, Gimli,
son of Glóin...

1123
01:41:36,757 --> 01:41:41,012
...by any craft that we here possess.

1124
01:41:41,505 --> 01:41:44,482
The Ring was made in the fires
of Mount Doom.

1125
01:41:44,506 --> 01:41:49,687
{\an8}THE RING: <i> In the Land of Mordor where the Shadows lie.
<font color="#bd2600">(Daghburz-ishi makha Gulshu darulu.)</font></i>

1126
01:41:45,850 --> 01:41:49,687
Only there can it be unmade.

1127
01:41:50,730 --> 01:41:53,357
It must be taken deep into Mordor...

1128
01:41:53,529 --> 01:41:56,862
...and cast back into the fiery chasm
from whence it came.

1129
01:41:56,887 --> 01:42:00,506
{\an8}THE RING: <i> In the Land of Mordor where the Shadows lie...
<font color="#bd2600">(Daghburz-ishi makha Gulshu darulu...)</font></i>

1130
01:42:00,531 --> 01:42:02,533
One of you...

1131
01:42:03,034 --> 01:42:05,202
...must do this.

1132
01:42:08,122 --> 01:42:11,834
One does not simply walk into Mordor.

1133
01:42:12,710 --> 01:42:16,380
Its Black Gates are guarded
by more than just Orcs.

1134
01:42:17,214 --> 01:42:21,344
There is evil there
that does not sleep.

1135
01:42:21,552 --> 01:42:25,765
The Great Eye is ever-watchful.

1136
01:42:26,557 --> 01:42:28,559
It is a barren wasteland...

1137
01:42:28,768 --> 01:42:32,396
...riddled with fire, and ash
and dust.

1138
01:42:32,563 --> 01:42:36,400
The very air you breathe
is a poisonous fume.

1139
01:42:36,651 --> 01:42:40,905
Not with 10,000 men
could you do this. It is folly.

1140
01:42:41,155 --> 01:42:45,576
Have you heard nothing Lord Elrond
has said? The Ring must be destroyed.

1141
01:42:45,785 --> 01:42:48,412
And I suppose you think
you are the one to do it!

1142
01:42:48,579 --> 01:42:53,250
And if we fail, what then? What happens
when Sauron takes back what is his?

1143
01:42:53,417 --> 01:42:58,756
I will be dead before I see the Ring
in the hands of an Elf!

1144
01:42:58,923 --> 01:43:00,549
[SHOUTING]

1145
01:43:00,758 --> 01:43:03,260
Never trust an Elf!

1146
01:43:04,361 --> 01:43:08,036
GANDALF:
Do you not understand? While you bicker amongst yourselves,

1147
01:43:08,061 --> 01:43:10,267
Sauron's power grows!

1148
01:43:08,063 --> 01:43:10,267
{\an8}THE RING: <i>One Ring to rule them all... <font color="#bd2600">(Ash Nazg durbatulûk...)</font></i>

1149
01:43:10,601 --> 01:43:13,553
None can escape it! You'll all be destroyed!

1150
01:43:10,599 --> 01:43:13,549
{\an8}<i>One Ring to find them... <font color="#bd2600">(Ash Nazg gimbatul...)</font></i>

1151
01:43:14,481 --> 01:43:16,787
{\an8}<i>One Ring to rule them all...
<font color="#bd2600">(Ash Nazg durbatulûk...)</font></i>

1152
01:43:16,812 --> 01:43:18,821
{\an8}<i>...One Ring to find them...
<font color="#bd2600">(...Ash Nazg gimbatul...)</font></i>

1153
01:43:18,845 --> 01:43:21,347
{\an8}<i>One Ring to rule them all...
<font color="#bd2600">(Ash Nazg durbatulûk...)</font></i>

1154
01:43:21,371 --> 01:43:23,534
{\an8}<i>...One Ring to find them...
<font color="#bd2600">(...Ash Nazg gimbatul...)</font></i>

1155
01:43:23,559 --> 01:43:25,729
{\an8}<i>One Ring to rule them all...
<font color="#bd2600">(Ash Nazg durbatulûk...)</font></i>

1156
01:43:25,753 --> 01:43:27,869
{\an8}<i>...One Ring to find them...
<font color="#bd2600">(...Ash Nazg gimbatul...)</font></i>

1157
01:43:27,893 --> 01:43:29,582
{\an8}<i>One Ring to rule them all...
<font color="#bd2600">(Ash Nazg durbatulûk...)</font></i>

1158
01:43:32,248 --> 01:43:34,458
I will take it.

1159
01:43:36,460 --> 01:43:38,963
I will take it.

1160
01:43:44,802 --> 01:43:47,847
I will take the Ring to Mordor.

1161
01:43:55,896 --> 01:43:57,148
Though...

1162
01:44:00,234 --> 01:44:02,069
...I do not know the way.

1163
01:44:04,071 --> 01:44:08,409
I will help you bear
this burden, Frodo Baggins...

1164
01:44:08,576 --> 01:44:11,954
...as long as it is yours to bear.

1165
01:44:13,080 --> 01:44:16,167
If by my life
or death I can protect you...

1166
01:44:16,917 --> 01:44:18,252
...I will.

1167
01:44:21,464 --> 01:44:23,758
You have my sword.

1168
01:44:25,593 --> 01:44:27,678
And you have my bow.

1169
01:44:28,262 --> 01:44:30,765
And my ax.

1170
01:44:37,772 --> 01:44:40,775
You carry the fates
of us all, little one.

1171
01:44:42,777 --> 01:44:46,447
If this is indeed
the will of the Council...

1172
01:44:46,906 --> 01:44:49,325
-...then Gondor will see it done.
-Hey!

1173
01:44:51,952 --> 01:44:56,707
-Frodo's not going anywhere without me.
-It is hardly possible to separate you...

1174
01:44:56,916 --> 01:45:01,796
...even when he is summoned
to a secret Council and you are not.

1175
01:45:02,296 --> 01:45:04,256
We're coming too!

1176
01:45:06,383 --> 01:45:09,136
You'll have to send us home
tied up in a sack to stop us.

1177
01:45:09,386 --> 01:45:12,723
Anyway, you need people
of intelligence on this sort of...

1178
01:45:13,057 --> 01:45:14,391
...mission.

1179
01:45:14,558 --> 01:45:16,060
Quest.

1180
01:45:16,519 --> 01:45:17,561
Thing.

1181
01:45:19,396 --> 01:45:22,066
Well, that rules you out, Pip.

1182
01:45:23,651 --> 01:45:25,569
Nine companions.

1183
01:45:27,404 --> 01:45:29,240
So be it.

1184
01:45:29,573 --> 01:45:32,576
You shall be
the Fellowship of the Ring.

1185
01:45:33,244 --> 01:45:35,079
Great!

1186
01:45:35,287 --> 01:45:37,581
Where are we going?

1187
01:46:13,123 --> 01:46:15,685
ELROND [IN SINDARIN]: <font color="#00bd00">(Anirne hene beriad i chên lîn...)</font>

1188
01:46:17,496 --> 01:46:21,326
<font color="#00bd00">(ned Imladris nauthant e le beriathar aen.)</font>

1189
01:46:23,654 --> 01:46:27,157
[IN WESTRON] In her heart, your mother
knew you'd be hunted all your life.

1190
01:46:27,658 --> 01:46:29,326
That you'd never escape your fate.

1191
01:46:29,826 --> 01:46:33,497
The skill of the Elves
can reforge the sword of kings...

1192
01:46:33,914 --> 01:46:37,834
...but only you have the power
to wield it.

1193
01:46:38,835 --> 01:46:41,338
I do not want that power.

1194
01:46:41,505 --> 01:46:44,174
I have never wanted it.

1195
01:46:45,509 --> 01:46:48,136
You are the last of that bloodline.
There is no other.

1196
01:46:52,516 --> 01:46:54,851
BILBO:
My old sword! Sting.

1197
01:46:55,060 --> 01:46:56,186
Here, take it. Take it.

1198
01:47:01,692 --> 01:47:05,654
-It's so light.
-Yes. Made by the Elves, you know.

1199
01:47:06,363 --> 01:47:10,450
The blade glows blue
when Orcs are close.

1200
01:47:10,659 --> 01:47:15,205
And it's times like that, my lad,
when you have to be extra careful.

1201
01:47:15,414 --> 01:47:17,874
Here's a pretty thing.

1202
01:47:18,291 --> 01:47:19,584
Mithril.

1203
01:47:20,377 --> 01:47:24,756
As light as a feather,
and as hard as dragon scales.

1204
01:47:24,965 --> 01:47:28,218
Let me see you put it on. Come on.

1205
01:47:31,763 --> 01:47:33,223
Oh!

1206
01:47:36,268 --> 01:47:38,311
My old ring.

1207
01:47:39,563 --> 01:47:43,483
I should very much like...

1208
01:47:43,734 --> 01:47:47,738
...to hold it again, one last time.

1209
01:48:05,088 --> 01:48:08,759
I'm sorry I brought this upon you,
my boy.

1210
01:48:09,092 --> 01:48:13,221
I'm sorry that you
must carry this burden.

1211
01:48:17,726 --> 01:48:20,771
I'm sorry for everything.

1212
01:48:35,744 --> 01:48:39,998
The Ring-bearer is setting out
on the Quest of Mount Doom.

1213
01:48:41,333 --> 01:48:43,960
On you who travel with him,
no oath...

1214
01:48:44,169 --> 01:48:47,297
...nor bond is laid to go further
than you will.

1215
01:48:50,759 --> 01:48:53,303
Farewell. Hold to your purpose.

1216
01:48:53,762 --> 01:48:57,682
May the blessings of Elves and Men...

1217
01:48:58,225 --> 01:49:00,811
...and all Free Folk go with you.

1218
01:49:03,897 --> 01:49:07,984
The Fellowship awaits the Ring-bearer.

1219
01:49:26,419 --> 01:49:28,922
Mordor, Gandalf, is it left or right?

1220
01:49:29,464 --> 01:49:31,299
Left.

1221
01:50:50,795 --> 01:50:55,217
GANDALF: <i> We must hold to this course,
west of the Misty Mountains, for 40 days.</i>

1222
01:50:55,425 --> 01:50:59,179
<i>If our luck holds, the Gap of Rohan
will still be open to us.</i>

1223
01:50:59,387 --> 01:51:02,933
<i>From there, our road
turns east to Mordor.</i>

1224
01:51:03,099 --> 01:51:06,937
Two, one, five. Good! Very good.

1225
01:51:08,772 --> 01:51:09,814
Move your feet.

1226
01:51:10,023 --> 01:51:11,358
MERRY: You look good, Pippin.
-Thanks.

1227
01:51:11,566 --> 01:51:12,943
BOROMIR:
Faster!

1228
01:51:14,319 --> 01:51:18,114
If anyone was to ask for my opinion,
which I note they're not...

1229
01:51:18,323 --> 01:51:21,076
...I'd say we were taking
the long way 'round.

1230
01:51:21,576 --> 01:51:24,621
Gandalf, we could pass through
the Mines of Moria.

1231
01:51:25,288 --> 01:51:29,125
My cousin Balin would give us
a royal welcome.

1232
01:51:29,459 --> 01:51:34,839
No, I would not take the road through
Moria unless I had no other choice.

1233
01:51:44,057 --> 01:51:45,141
Sorry!

1234
01:51:45,976 --> 01:51:47,477
MERRY:
Get him!

1235
01:51:48,812 --> 01:51:51,273
MERRY: For the Shire!
PIPPIN: Hold him. Hold him down, Merry!

1236
01:51:51,815 --> 01:51:54,150
Gentlemen, that's enough.

1237
01:51:57,946 --> 01:51:59,572
MERRY: You've got my arm!
You've got my arm!

1238
01:51:59,990 --> 01:52:02,659
-What is that?
-Nothing. It's just a wisp of cloud.

1239
01:52:02,909 --> 01:52:05,620
It's moving fast.

1240
01:52:05,829 --> 01:52:07,998
Against the wind.

1241
01:52:08,790 --> 01:52:10,917
-Crebain from Dunland!
-Hide!

1242
01:52:11,126 --> 01:52:13,837
-Hurry!
-Take cover!

1243
01:52:47,245 --> 01:52:48,997
Spies of Saruman.

1244
01:52:49,748 --> 01:52:53,043
The passage south is being watched.

1245
01:52:54,210 --> 01:52:57,547
We must take the Pass of Caradhras.

1246
01:53:10,185 --> 01:53:11,895
ARAGORN:
Frodo!

1247
01:53:30,865 --> 01:53:33,117
Boromir.

1248
01:53:33,375 --> 01:53:37,587
It is a strange fate that we should
suffer so much fear and doubt...

1249
01:53:37,795 --> 01:53:40,923
...over so small a thing.

1250
01:53:44,135 --> 01:53:46,096
Such a little thing.

1251
01:53:46,304 --> 01:53:47,764
Boromir!

1252
01:53:48,390 --> 01:53:51,101
Give the Ring to Frodo.

1253
01:54:00,902 --> 01:54:02,946
As you wish.

1254
01:54:03,655 --> 01:54:05,657
I care not.

1255
01:54:10,120 --> 01:54:12,455
[BOROMIR CHUCKLES]

1256
01:54:22,841 --> 01:54:25,635
[BIRDS SQUAWKING]

1257
01:54:41,067 --> 01:54:45,780
So, Gandalf, you try
to lead them over Caradhras.

1258
01:54:45,989 --> 01:54:50,577
And if that fails,
where then will you go?

1259
01:54:51,870 --> 01:54:54,831
<i>If the mountain defeats you...</i>

1260
01:54:55,081 --> 01:54:59,502
<i>...will you risk
a more dangerous road?</i>

1261
01:55:05,375 --> 01:55:07,245
{\an8}[SARUMAN CHANTS IN QUENYA]: <i> Wake up...
<font color="#0078bd">(Cuiva...)</font></i>

1262
01:55:07,507 --> 01:55:09,377
{\an8}[ECHOING]: <i>...cruel...
<font color="#0078bd">(...nwalca...)</font></i>

1263
01:55:09,749 --> 01:55:11,619
{\an8}<i>...Redhorn!
<font color="#0078bd">(...Carnirassë!)</font></i>

1264
01:55:11,848 --> 01:55:14,726
There is a fell voice on the air.

1265
01:55:12,048 --> 01:55:16,188
{\an8}<i>It shall fall upon the enemy's heads!
<font color="#0078bd">(Taltuva ñotto-carinnar!)</font></i>

1266
01:55:15,852 --> 01:55:17,353
It's Saruman!

1267
01:55:26,237 --> 01:55:30,909
He's trying to bring down the mountain!
Gandalf, we must turn back!

1268
01:55:31,201 --> 01:55:32,994
No!

1269
01:55:35,987 --> 01:55:38,955
[CHANTS IN SINDARIN] Sleep Caradhras, be still, lie still...
<font color="#00bd00">(Losto Caradhras, sedho, hodo...)</font>

1270
01:55:38,979 --> 01:55:41,306
...hold!
<font color="#00bd00">(...nuitho!)</font>

1271
01:55:40,550 --> 01:55:46,826
{\an8}SARUMAN: <i> Wake up cruel Redhorn!
<font color="#0078bd">(Cuiva nwalca Carnirassë!)</font></i>

1272
01:55:47,316 --> 01:55:50,474
May your blood-stained horn...
<font color="#0078bd">(Nai yarvaxëa rasselya...)</font>

1273
01:55:50,969 --> 01:55:54,237
...shall fall upon the enemy-heads!
<font color="#0078bd">(...taltuva ñotto-carinnar!)</font>

1274
01:55:55,901 --> 01:55:58,542
<i>Wake up cruel...
<font color="#0078bd">(Cuiva nwalca...)</font></i>

1275
01:55:59,574 --> 01:56:00,448
<i>...Redhorn!
<font color="#0078bd">(...Carnirassë!)</font></i>

1276
01:56:39,435 --> 01:56:41,271
We must get off the mountain!

1277
01:56:41,771 --> 01:56:46,109
Make for the Gap of Rohan,
and take the west road to my city!

1278
01:56:46,276 --> 01:56:49,612
The Gap of Rohan takes us
too close to Isengard!

1279
01:56:49,779 --> 01:56:53,533
GIMLI: We cannot pass over a mountain.
Let us go under it.

1280
01:56:53,783 --> 01:56:56,619
Let us go through the Mines of Moria.

1281
01:56:58,454 --> 01:57:02,292
SARUMAN: <i> Moria. You fear to go
into those mines.</i>

1282
01:57:02,959 --> 01:57:07,964
The Dwarves delved too greedily
and too deep.

1283
01:57:08,798 --> 01:57:13,678
<i>You know what they awoke
in the darkness of Khazad-dûm:</i>

1284
01:57:14,971 --> 01:57:18,474
Shadow and flame.

1285
01:57:21,811 --> 01:57:24,480
Let the Ring-bearer decide.

1286
01:57:29,193 --> 01:57:31,321
We cannot stay here!

1287
01:57:31,487 --> 01:57:34,324
This will be the death of the Hobbits.

1288
01:57:34,490 --> 01:57:36,200
Frodo?

1289
01:57:39,203 --> 01:57:42,081
We will go through the mines.

1290
01:57:42,832 --> 01:57:44,709
So be it.

1291
01:57:51,341 --> 01:57:55,303
Frodo, come and help an old man.

1292
01:57:58,848 --> 01:58:01,017
How is your shoulder?

1293
01:58:01,225 --> 01:58:04,520
-Better than it was.
-And the Ring?

1294
01:58:06,022 --> 01:58:08,524
You feel its power growing, don't you?

1295
01:58:09,025 --> 01:58:11,944
I've felt it too.
You must be careful now.

1296
01:58:12,362 --> 01:58:16,282
Evil will be drawn to you
from outside the Fellowship.

1297
01:58:16,449 --> 01:58:19,035
And, I fear, from within.

1298
01:58:21,704 --> 01:58:25,875
-Who then do I trust?
-You must trust yourself.

1299
01:58:26,042 --> 01:58:28,878
Trust your own strengths.

1300
01:58:29,045 --> 01:58:31,631
-What do you mean?
-There are many powers in this world...

1301
01:58:31,839 --> 01:58:33,883
...for good or for evil.

1302
01:58:34,050 --> 01:58:36,386
Some are greater than I am.

1303
01:58:36,886 --> 01:58:40,556
And against some I have not yet
been tested.

1304
01:58:41,891 --> 01:58:43,267
The walls...

1305
01:58:43,976 --> 01:58:46,062
...of Moria.

1306
01:58:51,776 --> 01:58:54,779
Dwarf doors are invisible when closed.

1307
01:58:54,804 --> 01:58:59,409
GANDALF: Yes Gimli, their own masters cannot find
them if their secrets are forgotten.

1308
01:58:59,784 --> 01:59:02,286
Why doesn't that surprise me?

1309
01:59:10,294 --> 01:59:13,589
Well, let's see.

1310
01:59:13,798 --> 01:59:15,174
Ithildin.

1311
01:59:15,800 --> 01:59:19,178
It mirrors only starlight
and moonlight.

1312
01:59:33,234 --> 01:59:37,321
It reads, "The Doors of Durin,
Lord of Moria.

1313
01:59:37,905 --> 01:59:42,535
-Speak, friend, and enter."
-What do you suppose that means?

1314
01:59:42,785 --> 01:59:47,540
It's simple. If you are a friend, you speak
the password and the doors will open.

1315
01:59:48,082 --> 01:59:52,429
[IN SINDARIN] Gate of the Elves, open now for me!
<font color="#00bd00">(Annon Edhellen, edro hi ammen.)</font>

1316
02:00:00,812 --> 02:00:07,214
Doorway of the Dwarf-folk, listen to the word of my tongue.
<font color="#00bd00">(Fennas Nogothrim, lasto beth lammen.)</font>

1317
02:00:11,314 --> 02:00:12,440
Nothing's happening.

1318
02:00:19,447 --> 02:00:23,659
I once knew every spell
in all the tongues of Elves...

1319
02:00:23,993 --> 02:00:26,829
...Men and Orcs.

1320
02:00:27,079 --> 02:00:28,331
What are you going to do, then?

1321
02:00:28,498 --> 02:00:30,750
Knock your head against these doors,
Peregrin Took!

1322
02:00:31,000 --> 02:00:33,002
And if that does not shatter them...

1323
02:00:33,169 --> 02:00:35,880
...and I am allowed a little peace
from foolish questions...

1324
02:00:36,042 --> 02:00:39,504
...I will try to find the opening words.

1325
02:00:39,661 --> 02:00:42,800
[GANDALF SPEAKS IN KHUZDÛL]

1326
02:00:43,065 --> 02:00:46,036
[IN SINDARIN] Gate of Elves...
<font color="#00bd00">(Ando Eldarinwa...)</font>

1327
02:00:46,709 --> 02:00:48,741
...listen to my word,
<font color="#00bd00">(...a lasta quettanya,)</font>

1328
02:00:49,616 --> 02:00:51,922
Threshold of Dwarves!
<font color="#00bd00">(Fenda Casarinwa!)</font>

1329
02:00:52,355 --> 02:00:54,899
Mines are no place for a pony.

1330
02:00:55,107 --> 02:00:58,787
-Even one so brave as Bill.
-Bye-bye, Bill.

1331
02:00:58,812 --> 02:01:00,338
GANDALF, SOFTLY: <i>Doorway of the Dwarf-folk...
<font color="#00bd00">(Fennas Nogothrim...)</font></i>

1332
02:01:00,363 --> 02:01:03,199
Go on, Bill. Go on.
GANDALF: <i> ...listen to the word of my tongue. <font color="#00bd00">(...lasto beth lammen.)</font></i>

1333
02:01:03,672 --> 02:01:07,244
Don't worry, Sam, he knows the way home.

1334
02:01:06,197 --> 02:01:07,686
GANDALF: <i> Gate of Elves... <font color="#00bd00">(Ando Eldarinwa...)</font></i>

1335
02:01:14,043 --> 02:01:16,629
Do not disturb the water.

1336
02:01:16,879 --> 02:01:18,714
Oh, it's useless.

1337
02:01:31,394 --> 02:01:33,563
It's a riddle.

1338
02:01:36,315 --> 02:01:39,443
"Speak 'friend' and enter."

1339
02:01:39,819 --> 02:01:42,738
What's the Elvish word for "friend"?

1340
02:01:44,240 --> 02:01:45,533
<i>Mellon.</i>

1341
02:02:03,593 --> 02:02:08,431
GIMLI: Soon, Master Elf, you will enjoy
the fabled hospitality of the Dwarves.

1342
02:02:08,931 --> 02:02:14,604
Roaring fires, malt beer,
ripe meat off the bone!

1343
02:02:16,105 --> 02:02:19,191
This, my friend,
is the home of my cousin Balin.

1344
02:02:19,567 --> 02:02:21,944
And they call it a mine.

1345
02:02:22,153 --> 02:02:24,113
A mine!

1346
02:02:25,156 --> 02:02:28,492
This is no mine. It's a tomb.

1347
02:02:32,788 --> 02:02:34,206
GIMLI:
No.

1348
02:02:34,624 --> 02:02:36,208
No...

1349
02:02:37,460 --> 02:02:39,128
No!

1350
02:02:41,797 --> 02:02:43,299
Goblins.

1351
02:02:47,219 --> 02:02:51,515
We make for the Gap of Rohan.
We should never have come here.

1352
02:02:52,600 --> 02:02:55,144
ARAGORN:
Now, get out of here. Get out!

1353
02:02:57,980 --> 02:03:00,316
MERRY: Frodo!
FRODO: Help!

1354
02:03:00,524 --> 02:03:02,151
Strider!

1355
02:03:02,318 --> 02:03:05,154
FRODO: Help!
SAM: Get off him!

1356
02:03:05,321 --> 02:03:06,322
Aragorn!

1357
02:03:16,749 --> 02:03:17,833
Frodo!

1358
02:03:19,001 --> 02:03:20,544
Strider!

1359
02:03:44,151 --> 02:03:45,194
Into the mines!

1360
02:03:45,361 --> 02:03:48,572
-Legolas!
ARAGORN: Into the cave!

1361
02:03:52,868 --> 02:03:54,662
Run!

1362
02:04:11,554 --> 02:04:15,099
GANDALF:
We now have but one choice.

1363
02:04:15,307 --> 02:04:20,229
We must face the long dark of Moria.

1364
02:04:20,438 --> 02:04:22,398
Be on your guard.

1365
02:04:22,606 --> 02:04:26,068
There are older
and fouler things than Orcs...

1366
02:04:26,235 --> 02:04:29,780
...in the deep places of the world.

1367
02:04:37,747 --> 02:04:41,709
Quietly now. It's a four-day journey
to the other side.

1368
02:04:41,917 --> 02:04:45,755
Let us hope that our presence
may go unnoticed.

1369
02:05:31,509 --> 02:05:35,221
The wealth of Moria is not in gold...

1370
02:05:35,387 --> 02:05:37,807
...or jewels...

1371
02:05:37,973 --> 02:05:41,018
...but mithril.

1372
02:05:59,370 --> 02:06:04,291
Bilbo had a shirt of mithril rings
that Thorin gave him.

1373
02:06:04,500 --> 02:06:08,504
-Oh, that was a kingly gift.
-Yes.

1374
02:06:08,671 --> 02:06:10,548
I never told him...

1375
02:06:10,714 --> 02:06:15,678
...but its worth was greater than
the value of the Shire.

1376
02:06:28,023 --> 02:06:29,733
Pippin.

1377
02:06:50,421 --> 02:06:53,048
I have no memory of this place.

1378
02:06:55,134 --> 02:06:56,635
PIPPIN: Are we lost?
MERRY: No.

1379
02:06:56,844 --> 02:06:59,346
PIPPIN: I think we are.
MERRY: Gandalf's thinking.

1380
02:06:59,555 --> 02:07:00,973
PIPPIN: Merry?
MERRY: What?

1381
02:07:01,265 --> 02:07:03,225
PIPPIN:
I'm hungry.

1382
02:07:14,528 --> 02:07:18,991
-There's something down there.
-It's Gollum.

1383
02:07:19,200 --> 02:07:23,329
-Gollum?
-He's been following us for three days.

1384
02:07:23,537 --> 02:07:27,708
-He escaped the dungeons of Barad-dûr?
-Escaped...

1385
02:07:28,375 --> 02:07:30,044
...or was set loose.

1386
02:07:30,544 --> 02:07:34,215
Now the Ring has brought him here.

1387
02:07:36,842 --> 02:07:39,595
He will never be rid of his need for it.

1388
02:07:39,762 --> 02:07:45,517
He hates and loves the Ring,
as he hates and loves himself.

1389
02:07:45,684 --> 02:07:50,564
Sméagol's life is a sad story.

1390
02:07:50,731 --> 02:07:56,695
Yes, Sméagol he was once called.
Before the Ring found him.

1391
02:07:57,613 --> 02:08:00,407
Before it drove him mad.

1392
02:08:00,699 --> 02:08:03,577
It's a pity Bilbo didn't kill him
when he had the chance.

1393
02:08:03,744 --> 02:08:04,954
Pity?

1394
02:08:06,038 --> 02:08:08,916
It is pity that stayed Bilbo's hand.

1395
02:08:09,833 --> 02:08:15,047
Many that live deserve death.
Some that die deserve life.

1396
02:08:16,465 --> 02:08:18,968
Can you give it to them, Frodo?

1397
02:08:21,387 --> 02:08:25,349
Do not be too eager
to deal out death and judgment.

1398
02:08:25,557 --> 02:08:28,477
Even the very wise
cannot see all ends.

1399
02:08:29,061 --> 02:08:34,984
My heart tells me that Gollum has some
part to play yet, for good or ill...

1400
02:08:35,776 --> 02:08:38,612
...before this is over.

1401
02:08:40,114 --> 02:08:43,993
The pity of Bilbo
may rule the fate of many.

1402
02:08:50,624 --> 02:08:54,003
I wish the Ring
had never come to me.

1403
02:08:55,421 --> 02:08:57,464
I wish none of this had happened.

1404
02:08:57,631 --> 02:09:02,678
So do all who live to see such times.
But that is not for them to decide.

1405
02:09:03,512 --> 02:09:09,018
All we have to decide is what to do
with the time that is given to us.

1406
02:09:10,519 --> 02:09:14,523
There are other forces at work in this
world, Frodo, besides the will of evil.

1407
02:09:14,898 --> 02:09:17,318
Bilbo was meant to find the Ring.

1408
02:09:17,818 --> 02:09:22,156
In which case,
you also were meant to have it.

1409
02:09:22,323 --> 02:09:25,534
And that is an encouraging thought.

1410
02:09:28,454 --> 02:09:29,621
Ah!

1411
02:09:30,414 --> 02:09:32,333
It's that way.

1412
02:09:32,541 --> 02:09:34,835
-He's remembered.
GANDALF: No.

1413
02:09:35,044 --> 02:09:38,839
But the air doesn't smell
so foul down here.

1414
02:09:39,048 --> 02:09:44,219
If in doubt, Meriadoc,
always follow your nose.

1415
02:09:59,068 --> 02:10:03,197
Let me risk a little more light.

1416
02:10:07,868 --> 02:10:09,953
Behold...

1417
02:10:10,371 --> 02:10:15,584
...the great realm
and Dwarf-city of Dwarrowdelf.

1418
02:10:18,087 --> 02:10:21,507
There's an eye opener, and no mistake.

1419
02:10:46,407 --> 02:10:48,117
Gimli!

1420
02:10:53,914 --> 02:10:55,374
No.

1421
02:10:55,582 --> 02:10:57,209
No!

1422
02:10:59,753 --> 02:11:02,923
Oh, no.

1423
02:11:04,758 --> 02:11:06,051
No.

1424
02:11:13,308 --> 02:11:15,310
GANDALF:
"Here lies Balin...

1425
02:11:15,769 --> 02:11:17,771
...son of Fundin...

1426
02:11:18,105 --> 02:11:20,732
...Lord of Moria."

1427
02:11:21,775 --> 02:11:23,444
He is dead, then.

1428
02:11:25,612 --> 02:11:26,822
It's as I feared.

1429
02:11:34,738 --> 02:11:37,599
GIMLI, SOFTLY [IN KHUZDÛL]: <i> A crown of rust in the waters...
<font color="#bd4500">(Kilmîn malur ni zâram...)</font></i>

1430
02:11:37,624 --> 02:11:43,353
<i>...cold and black, of the Kheled-zâram. Balin sleeps.
<font color="#bd4500">(...kalil ra narag, Kheled-zâram... Balin tazlifi.)</font></i>

1431
02:11:45,132 --> 02:11:48,051
We must move on. We cannot linger.

1432
02:11:48,260 --> 02:11:52,973
GANDALF: "They have taken the bridge
and the second hall.

1433
02:11:54,057 --> 02:11:56,643
We have barred the gates...

1434
02:11:57,311 --> 02:11:59,813
...but cannot hold them for long.

1435
02:11:59,980 --> 02:12:02,816
The ground shakes.

1436
02:12:03,192 --> 02:12:04,818
Drums...

1437
02:12:05,194 --> 02:12:08,572
...drums in the deep.

1438
02:12:12,117 --> 02:12:14,161
We cannot get out.

1439
02:12:16,163 --> 02:12:20,000
A Shadow moves in the dark.

1440
02:12:21,668 --> 02:12:24,213
We cannot get out.

1441
02:12:27,216 --> 02:12:29,176
They are coming."

1442
02:12:32,387 --> 02:12:34,223
[CLATTERING]

1443
02:12:51,615 --> 02:12:54,910
[THUDDING]

1444
02:13:00,832 --> 02:13:02,584
[SILENCE]

1445
02:13:12,219 --> 02:13:14,054
Fool of a Took!

1446
02:13:14,388 --> 02:13:18,225
Throw yourself in next time,
and rid us of your stupidity.

1447
02:13:21,853 --> 02:13:24,731
[DRUMS BEATING]

1448
02:13:34,950 --> 02:13:37,286
[SCREECHING]

1449
02:13:44,167 --> 02:13:45,794
SAM:
Frodo!

1450
02:13:48,088 --> 02:13:49,590
Orcs.

1451
02:13:56,638 --> 02:13:58,640
Get back! Stay close to Gandalf!

1452
02:14:05,897 --> 02:14:07,691
They have a cave-troll.

1453
02:14:23,498 --> 02:14:24,666
Let them come!

1454
02:14:25,167 --> 02:14:28,712
There is one Dwarf yet in Moria
who still draws breath.

1455
02:14:43,852 --> 02:14:45,729
[SCREECHES]

1456
02:16:47,601 --> 02:16:50,353
I think I'm getting the hang of this.

1457
02:16:55,108 --> 02:16:56,777
Frodo!

1458
02:17:30,310 --> 02:17:32,145
FRODO:
Aragorn! Aragorn!

1459
02:17:33,146 --> 02:17:35,023
Frodo!

1460
02:18:20,193 --> 02:18:22,070
Frodo!

1461
02:18:24,865 --> 02:18:26,324
Frodo!

1462
02:19:22,297 --> 02:19:23,632
Oh, no.

1463
02:19:26,468 --> 02:19:27,928
[FRODO GROANS]

1464
02:19:32,015 --> 02:19:33,892
He's alive.

1465
02:19:36,311 --> 02:19:39,314
I'm all right. I'm not hurt.

1466
02:19:39,648 --> 02:19:41,816
You should be dead.

1467
02:19:42,025 --> 02:19:44,527
That spear would have skewered
a wild boar.

1468
02:19:44,778 --> 02:19:49,532
I think there's more to this Hobbit
than meets the eye.

1469
02:19:55,330 --> 02:19:56,456
Mithril.

1470
02:19:59,250 --> 02:20:01,836
You are full of surprises,
Master Baggins.

1471
02:20:02,337 --> 02:20:05,298
[SCREECHING]

1472
02:20:07,842 --> 02:20:09,803
To the Bridge of Khazad-dûm!

1473
02:20:24,776 --> 02:20:26,361
ARAGORN:
This way!

1474
02:21:09,988 --> 02:21:12,032
[GROWLING]

1475
02:21:36,765 --> 02:21:39,768
What is this new devilry?

1476
02:21:47,561 --> 02:21:52,160
{\an8}[CHORUS SINGS IN KHUZDÛL]: <i> The demon comes!
<font color="#bd4500">(Urkhas tanakhi!)</font></i>

1477
02:21:52,185 --> 02:21:58,283
{\an8}<i>The earth shakes!
<font color="#bd4500">(Kâmin takalladi!)</font></i>

1478
02:21:53,907 --> 02:21:55,700
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

1479
02:21:55,867 --> 02:21:58,661
A Balrog.

1480
02:21:58,885 --> 02:22:06,753
{\an8}<i>Fear rips our heart!
<font color="#bd4500">(Ugrûd tashniki kurdumâ!)</font></i>

1481
02:21:58,953 --> 02:22:02,123
A demon of the ancient world.

1482
02:22:04,292 --> 02:22:06,753
This foe is beyond any of you.

1483
02:22:07,921 --> 02:22:09,464
Run!

1484
02:22:07,964 --> 02:22:09,464
{\an8}<i>Fire in the deep!
<font color="#bd4500">(Urus ni buzra!)</font></i>

1485
02:22:09,488 --> 02:22:10,988
{\an8}<i>The demon comes!
<font color="#bd4500">(Urkhas tanakhi!)</font></i>

1486
02:22:11,013 --> 02:22:12,387
{\an8}<i>No! No! No! No!
<font color="#bd4500">(Lu! Lu! Lu! Lu!)</font></i>

1487
02:22:12,416 --> 02:22:13,771
{\an8}<i>Fire in, fire in
<font color="#bd4500">(Urus ni, urus ni)</font></i>

1488
02:22:13,795 --> 02:22:15,141
{\an8}<i>Fire in the deep!
<font color="#bd4500">(Urus ni buzra!)</font></i>

1489
02:22:15,165 --> 02:22:16,780
{\an8}<i>Firey deep!
<font color="#bd4500">(Urus buzra!)</font></i>

1490
02:22:16,805 --> 02:22:18,306
Quickly!

1491
02:22:28,393 --> 02:22:33,381
{\an8}<i>Flames!
<font color="#bd4500">(Arrâs!)</font></i>

1492
02:22:34,948 --> 02:22:36,199
Gandalf.

1493
02:22:36,825 --> 02:22:38,451
Lead them on, Aragorn.

1494
02:22:39,828 --> 02:22:42,330
The bridge is near.

1495
02:22:41,524 --> 02:22:47,626
{\an8}<i>Flames!
<font color="#bd4500">(Arrâs!)</font></i>

1496
02:22:42,580 --> 02:22:44,207
[BALROG GROWLS]

1497
02:22:44,415 --> 02:22:48,503
Do as I say!
Swords are no more use here.

1498
02:23:03,346 --> 02:23:07,346
{\an8}<i>Flames!
<font color="#bd4500">(Arrâs!)</font></i>

1499
02:23:17,657 --> 02:23:19,367
Gandalf!

1500
02:23:37,677 --> 02:23:38,887
BOROMIR:
Merry! Pippin!

1501
02:23:50,023 --> 02:23:51,566
Sam!

1502
02:23:54,277 --> 02:23:57,530
Nobody tosses a Dwarf.

1503
02:24:00,575 --> 02:24:01,993
Not the beard!

1504
02:24:15,215 --> 02:24:17,091
Steady.

1505
02:24:19,219 --> 02:24:20,887
Hold on!

1506
02:24:23,848 --> 02:24:25,725
[BALROG GROWLS]

1507
02:24:26,809 --> 02:24:28,728
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

1508
02:24:27,492 --> 02:24:32,742
{\an8}<i>Flames lick our skin, our skin!
<font color="#bd4500">(Arrâs talbabi fillumâ, fillumâ!)</font></i>

1509
02:24:33,104 --> 02:24:38,604
{\an8}<i>Fear rips our heart, our heart!
<font color="#bd4500">(Ugrûd tashniki kurdumâ, kurdumâ!)</font></i>

1510
02:24:38,936 --> 02:24:41,467
{\an8}<i>The fire demon!
<font color="#bd4500">(Urus urkhas!)</font></i>

1511
02:24:41,491 --> 02:24:44,526
{\an8}<i>The demon comes! [Repeated]
<font color="#bd4500">(Urkhas tanakhi!)</font></i>

1512
02:24:41,950 --> 02:24:43,117
Hang on!

1513
02:24:44,543 --> 02:24:47,357
{\an8}<i>The earth shakes!
<font color="#bd4500">(Kâmin takalladi!)</font></i>

1514
02:24:47,381 --> 02:24:50,097
{\an8}<i>A great shadow!
<font color="#bd4500">(Askad gabil!)</font></i>

1515
02:24:50,121 --> 02:24:51,566
{\an8}<i>Fire!
<font color="#bd4500">(Urus!)</font></i>

1516
02:24:51,590 --> 02:24:54,590
{\an8}<i>The demon comes! [Repeated]
<font color="#bd4500">(Urkhas tanakhi!)</font></i>

1517
02:24:53,920 --> 02:24:55,630
Lean forward!

1518
02:24:54,615 --> 02:24:55,719
{\an8}<i>The earth shakes!
<font color="#bd4500">(Kâmin takalladi!)</font></i>

1519
02:24:55,743 --> 02:24:58,732
{\an8}<i>Fear rips our heart!
<font color="#bd4500">(Ugrûd tashniki kurdumâ!)</font></i>

1520
02:24:58,633 --> 02:24:59,634
Steady.

1521
02:24:58,758 --> 02:25:02,368
{\an8}<i>Demon fire!
<font color="#bd4500">(Urkhas urus!)</font></i>

1522
02:25:00,969 --> 02:25:02,136
Come on!

1523
02:25:02,387 --> 02:25:03,888
Now!

1524
02:25:21,114 --> 02:25:22,907
Over the bridge!

1525
02:25:23,157 --> 02:25:24,659
Fly!

1526
02:26:09,370 --> 02:26:11,372
You cannot pass!

1527
02:26:11,539 --> 02:26:13,207
Gandalf!

1528
02:26:17,420 --> 02:26:22,300
I am a servant of the Secret Fire,
wielder of the flame of Anor.

1529
02:26:23,301 --> 02:26:27,055
The dark fire will not avail you,
flame of Udûn!

1530
02:26:37,065 --> 02:26:39,067
Go back to the Shadow.

1531
02:26:46,908 --> 02:26:51,329
You shall not pass!

1532
02:27:18,481 --> 02:27:22,360
BOROMIR: No! No!
-Gandalf!

1533
02:27:30,034 --> 02:27:32,495
Fly, you fools!

1534
02:27:36,624 --> 02:27:38,793
No!

1535
02:27:44,966 --> 02:27:47,135
Aragorn!

1536
02:28:44,358 --> 02:28:47,195
Legolas, get them up.

1537
02:28:51,324 --> 02:28:53,159
Give them a moment, for pity's sake!

1538
02:28:53,326 --> 02:28:56,954
By nightfall, these hills will
be swarming with Orcs.

1539
02:28:57,163 --> 02:29:00,500
We must reach the woods of Lothlórien.

1540
02:29:01,375 --> 02:29:04,712
Come, Boromir. Legolas.
Gimli, get them up.

1541
02:29:06,214 --> 02:29:08,382
On your feet, Sam.

1542
02:29:08,716 --> 02:29:10,218
Frodo?

1543
02:29:12,303 --> 02:29:14,013
Frodo!

1544
02:30:06,524 --> 02:30:09,068
Stay close, young Hobbits!

1545
02:30:09,777 --> 02:30:13,948
They say that a great sorceress
lives in these woods.

1546
02:30:14,156 --> 02:30:16,701
An Elf-witch...

1547
02:30:17,243 --> 02:30:20,121
...of terrible power.

1548
02:30:20,663 --> 02:30:22,873
All who look upon her...

1549
02:30:23,082 --> 02:30:24,875
...fall under her spell.

1550
02:30:25,084 --> 02:30:26,377
GALADRIEL:
<i>Frodo!</i>

1551
02:30:28,629 --> 02:30:30,673
And are never seen again.

1552
02:30:30,881 --> 02:30:35,386
GALADRIEL: <i> Your coming to us is
as the footsteps of doom.</i>

1553
02:30:35,595 --> 02:30:39,307
<i>You bring great evil here,
Ring-bearer.</i>

1554
02:30:39,473 --> 02:30:41,267
SAM:
Mr. Frodo?

1555
02:30:46,564 --> 02:30:52,153
Well, here's one Dwarf
she won't ensnare so easily.

1556
02:30:52,320 --> 02:30:56,907
I have the eyes of a hawk
and the ears of a fox.

1557
02:31:04,582 --> 02:31:09,170
The Dwarf breathes so loud,
we could have shot him in the dark.

1558
02:31:14,314 --> 02:31:16,385
[IN SINDARIN] <font color="#00bd00">(Mae govannen, Legolas Thranduilion.)</font>

1559
02:31:17,276 --> 02:31:19,972
<font color="#00bd00">(Govannas vîn gwennen le, Haldir o Lórien.)</font>

1560
02:31:22,704 --> 02:31:24,480
<font color="#00bd00">(A Aragorn in Dúnedain...)</font>

1561
02:31:25,079 --> 02:31:26,517
<font color="#00bd00">(istannen le ammen.)</font>

1562
02:31:26,960 --> 02:31:27,638
Haldir.

1563
02:31:27,663 --> 02:31:29,607
So much for the legendary courtesy
of the Elves!

1564
02:31:29,774 --> 02:31:31,692
Speak words we can all understand!

1565
02:31:31,859 --> 02:31:36,447
[IN WESTRON] We have not had dealings
with the Dwarves since the Dark Days.

1566
02:31:36,697 --> 02:31:39,241
And you know what this Dwarf
says to that?

1567
02:31:39,516 --> 02:31:41,156
GIMLI [IN KHUZDÛL]: <i> May my excrement be poured...
<font color="#bd4500">(Îsh kakhfê...)</font></i>

1568
02:31:41,181 --> 02:31:43,611
...upon the naked-jawed [beardless].
<font color="#bd4500">(...ai-'d-dûr-rugnul.)</font>

1569
02:31:46,165 --> 02:31:48,125
That was not so courteous.

1570
02:31:54,674 --> 02:31:58,719
You bring great evil with you.

1571
02:32:00,471 --> 02:32:02,682
You can go no further.

1572
02:32:08,323 --> 02:32:09,737
ARAGORN [URGENTLY IN SINDARIN]: We need your protection.
<font color="#00bd00">(Boe ammen veriad lîn.)</font>

1573
02:32:09,761 --> 02:32:11,366
The road is fell!
<font color="#00bd00">(Andelu i ven!)</font>

1574
02:32:14,789 --> 02:32:15,687
I'm glad we came to you.
<font color="#00bd00">(Merin le telim.)</font>

1575
02:32:16,872 --> 02:32:18,559
We need your support!
<font color="#00bd00">(Boe ammen i dulu lîn!)</font>

1576
02:32:19,763 --> 02:32:21,319
HALDIR:
<i>Aragorn...</i>

1577
02:32:31,793 --> 02:32:33,136
HALDIR: <i> ...Eärendil.
<font color="#00bd00">(...Eärendil.)</font></i>

1578
02:32:33,161 --> 02:32:34,595
ARAGORN: <i> I'm glad we came to you.
<font color="#00bd00">(Merin le telim.)</font></i>

1579
02:32:37,658 --> 02:32:38,739
The road is deadly.
<font color="#00bd00">(Andelu i ven.)</font>

1580
02:32:39,927 --> 02:32:42,596
Gandalf's death was not in vain.

1581
02:32:43,723 --> 02:32:45,599
Nor would he have you give up hope.

1582
02:32:47,101 --> 02:32:50,438
You carry a heavy burden, Frodo.

1583
02:32:51,313 --> 02:32:54,442
Don't carry the weight of the dead.

1584
02:32:57,403 --> 02:32:59,447
You will follow me.

1585
02:33:11,125 --> 02:33:13,127
Caras Galadhon.

1586
02:33:13,753 --> 02:33:16,714
The heart of Elvendom on earth.

1587
02:33:16,881 --> 02:33:22,553
Realm of the Lord Celeborn
and of Galadriel, Lady of Light.

1588
02:33:22,905 --> 02:33:34,112
{\an8}[CHORUS SINGS IN QUENYA]: <i> Behold the light!
<font color="#0078bd">(Ela i cále!)</font></i>

1589
02:33:34,136 --> 02:33:45,333
{\an8}<i>Nenya is this
<font color="#0078bd">(Nenya sina)</font></i>

1590
02:33:45,624 --> 02:34:02,457
{\an8}<i>Ring, unbreakable
<font color="#0078bd">(Corma, úhátima)</font></i>

1591
02:34:02,487 --> 02:34:34,596
{\an8}<i>That I possess.
<font color="#0078bd">(I haryanye.)</font></i>

1592
02:34:41,549 --> 02:34:44,677
The enemy knows you have entered here.

1593
02:34:45,344 --> 02:34:50,516
What hope you had in secrecy
is now gone.

1594
02:34:52,226 --> 02:34:56,689
Eight there are here, yet nine there
were set out from Rivendell.

1595
02:34:56,939 --> 02:34:58,732
Tell me, where is Gandalf?

1596
02:34:58,941 --> 02:35:02,069
For I much desire to speak with him.

1597
02:35:02,236 --> 02:35:05,030
I can no longer see him from afar.

1598
02:35:05,906 --> 02:35:11,078
GALADRIEL: Gandalf the Grey did not
pass the borders of this land.

1599
02:35:11,328 --> 02:35:13,747
He has fallen into Shadow.

1600
02:35:18,460 --> 02:35:22,965
He was taken by both Shadow and flame.

1601
02:35:24,592 --> 02:35:28,345
A Balrog of Morgoth.

1602
02:35:29,054 --> 02:35:32,433
For we went needlessly
into the net of Moria.

1603
02:35:34,560 --> 02:35:37,771
Needless were none of the deeds
of Gandalf in life.

1604
02:35:38,439 --> 02:35:41,734
We do not yet know his full purpose.

1605
02:35:46,488 --> 02:35:50,784
Do not let the great emptiness
of Khazad-dûm fill your heart...

1606
02:35:51,076 --> 02:35:53,412
...Gimli, son of Glóin.

1607
02:35:54,413 --> 02:35:57,958
For the world has grown
full of peril...

1608
02:35:59,418 --> 02:36:02,087
...and in all lands...

1609
02:36:02,254 --> 02:36:05,758
...love is now mingled with grief.

1610
02:36:18,395 --> 02:36:21,106
What now becomes of this Fellowship?

1611
02:36:21,649 --> 02:36:24,652
Without Gandalf, hope is lost.

1612
02:36:27,613 --> 02:36:30,908
The quest stands upon the edge
of a knife.

1613
02:36:31,075 --> 02:36:34,161
Stray but a little and it will fail...

1614
02:36:34,912 --> 02:36:37,748
...to the ruin of all.

1615
02:36:42,086 --> 02:36:47,925
Yet hope remains
while the Company is true.

1616
02:36:49,468 --> 02:36:54,181
Do not let your hearts be troubled.
Go now and rest...

1617
02:36:54,640 --> 02:36:58,310
...for you are weary with sorrow
and much toil.

1618
02:37:00,562 --> 02:37:02,690
Tonight, you will sleep...

1619
02:37:02,856 --> 02:37:06,276
GALADRIEL:
<i>Welcome, Frodo of the Shire...</i>

1620
02:37:07,861 --> 02:37:09,655
<i>...one who has seen the Eye!</i>

1621
02:37:11,149 --> 02:37:15,423
{\an8}[SINGING IN SINDARIN]: <i> The bonds cut,
<font color="#00bd00">(In gwidh ristennin,)</font></i>

1622
02:37:15,468 --> 02:37:29,868
{\an8}[CHORUS IN QUENYA]: <i> Our regret is undying <font color="#0078bd">(Ilfirin nairelma)</font></i>

1623
02:37:21,728 --> 02:37:30,529
{\an8}<i>the spirit rent. <font color="#00bd00">(i fae narchannen.)</font></i>

1624
02:37:24,563 --> 02:37:26,311
A lament for Gandalf.

1625
02:37:29,853 --> 02:37:39,378
{\an8}<i>[CHORUS] What should be shall be. <font color="#0078bd">(Nauva i nauva.)</font></i>

1626
02:37:34,138 --> 02:37:35,681
What do they say about him?

1627
02:37:35,889 --> 02:37:37,656
I have not the heart to tell you.

1628
02:37:34,380 --> 02:37:39,278
{\an8}<i>The Flame of Anor, <font color="#00bd00">(I lach Anor,)</font></i>

1629
02:37:39,290 --> 02:37:56,406
{\an8}<i>from earth departed <font color="#00bd00">(ed ardhon gwannen)</font></i>

1630
02:37:41,663 --> 02:37:43,564
For me, the grief is still too near.

1631
02:37:42,348 --> 02:37:54,068
{\an8}<i>[CHORUS] Our regret is undying <font color="#0078bd">(Ilfirin nairelma)</font></i>

1632
02:37:46,756 --> 02:37:48,356
I bet they don't mention his fireworks.

1633
02:37:49,817 --> 02:37:51,228
There should be a verse about them.

1634
02:37:54,093 --> 02:38:19,714
{\an8}<i>[CHORUS] Rather than submit <font color="#0078bd">(Ar ullume nucuvalme)</font></i>

1635
02:37:56,431 --> 02:37:58,120
<i>The finest rockets ever seen</i>

1636
02:37:58,640 --> 02:38:10,216
{\an8}<i>Mithrandir! O Pilgrim Grey! <font color="#00bd00">(Mithrandir! A Randir Vithren!)</font></i>

1637
02:37:59,541 --> 02:38:01,922
<i>They burst in stars of blue and green</i>

1638
02:38:03,243 --> 02:38:04,148
SAM:
<i>Or after thunder,</i>

1639
02:38:05,709 --> 02:38:06,645
SAM:
<i>silver showers</i>

1640
02:38:09,215 --> 02:38:11,717
SAM:
<i>Came falling like a rain of flowers</i>

1641
02:38:11,884 --> 02:38:14,208
Oh, that doesn't do them justice
by a long road.

1642
02:38:11,422 --> 02:38:19,461
{\an8}<i>You will not wander <font color="#00bd00">(Ú-reniathach)</font></i>

1643
02:38:19,733 --> 02:38:24,031
{\an8}<i>[CHORUS] What should be shall be. <font color="#0078bd">(Nauva i nauva.)</font></i>

1644
02:38:24,062 --> 02:38:34,035
{\an8}<i>the green earth <font color="#00bd00">(i amar galen)</font></i>

1645
02:38:24,064 --> 02:38:40,723
{\an8}<i>[CHORUS] Our love for this land<font color="#0078bd">([Mel]melma nóren sina)</font></i>

1646
02:38:26,915 --> 02:38:27,892
ARAGORN:
Take some rest.

1647
02:38:29,707 --> 02:38:32,154
These borders are well-protected.

1648
02:38:32,362 --> 02:38:34,035
I will find no rest here.

1649
02:38:36,395 --> 02:38:46,959
{\an8}<i>Your journey in darkness, has ended. <font color="#00bd00">(I reniad lín ne môr, nuithannen.)</font></i>

1650
02:38:37,743 --> 02:38:39,299
I heard her voice inside my head.

1651
02:38:40,740 --> 02:38:48,835
{\an8}<i>[CHORUS] Submit...<font color="#0078bd">(Nucuvalme)</font></i>

1652
02:38:41,242 --> 02:38:43,368
She spoke of my father
and the fall of Gondor.

1653
02:38:44,918 --> 02:38:49,390
She said to me,
"Even now there is hope left."

1654
02:38:48,844 --> 02:38:58,521
{\an8}<i>[CHORUS] Our regret is undying. <font color="#0078bd">(Ilfirin nairelma.)</font></i>

1655
02:38:52,205 --> 02:38:53,216
But I cannot see it.

1656
02:38:56,215 --> 02:38:58,521
It is long since we had any hope.

1657
02:38:58,545 --> 02:39:07,505
{\an8}<i>[CHORUS] Rather than submit <font color="#0078bd">(Ar ullume nucuvalme)</font></i>

1658
02:39:08,607 --> 02:39:10,734
My father is a noble man.

1659
02:39:11,485 --> 02:39:13,737
But his rule is failing...

1660
02:39:14,071 --> 02:39:19,493
...and our people lose faith.

1661
02:39:20,911 --> 02:39:24,456
He looks to me to make things right,
and I would do it.

1662
02:39:24,623 --> 02:39:28,168
I would see the glory
of Gondor restored.

1663
02:39:31,004 --> 02:39:34,007
Have you ever seen it, Aragorn?

1664
02:39:34,633 --> 02:39:36,677
The White Tower of Ecthelion.

1665
02:39:36,844 --> 02:39:40,681
Glimmering like a spike
of pearl and silver.

1666
02:39:41,348 --> 02:39:44,852
Its banners caught high
in the morning breeze.

1667
02:39:47,729 --> 02:39:49,690
Have you ever been called home...

1668
02:39:49,857 --> 02:39:53,819
...by the clear ringing
of silver trumpets?

1669
02:39:54,444 --> 02:39:57,698
I have seen the White City...

1670
02:39:58,031 --> 02:39:59,533
...long ago.

1671
02:40:00,492 --> 02:40:05,455
One day, our paths will lead us there.

1672
02:40:06,373 --> 02:40:09,334
And the tower guard
shall take up the call:

1673
02:40:09,793 --> 02:40:13,130
"The Lords of Gondor have returned."

1674
02:41:20,322 --> 02:41:22,866
Will you look into the mirror?

1675
02:41:23,033 --> 02:41:24,576
What will I see?

1676
02:41:27,524 --> 02:41:29,860
Even the wisest cannot tell.

1677
02:41:30,791 --> 02:41:32,626
For the mirror...

1678
02:41:32,834 --> 02:41:35,379
...shows many things.

1679
02:41:38,382 --> 02:41:40,759
Things that were...

1680
02:41:40,968 --> 02:41:43,553
...things that are...

1681
02:41:44,304 --> 02:41:46,265
...and some things...

1682
02:41:49,851 --> 02:41:53,146
...that have not yet come to pass.

1683
02:42:57,044 --> 02:42:59,546
[VOICES SPEAKING IN BLACK SPEECH]

1684
02:43:15,729 --> 02:43:18,565
I know what it is you saw.

1685
02:43:20,984 --> 02:43:23,487
For it is also in my mind.

1686
02:43:25,238 --> 02:43:29,326
<i>It is what will come to pass
if you should fail.</i>

1687
02:43:31,703 --> 02:43:36,583
<i>The Fellowship is breaking.
It is already begun.</i>

1688
02:43:37,209 --> 02:43:40,504
<i>He will try to take the Ring.</i>

1689
02:43:40,712 --> 02:43:42,714
<i>You know of whom I speak.</i>

1690
02:43:43,715 --> 02:43:48,387
<i>One by one, it will destroy them all.</i>

1691
02:43:49,888 --> 02:43:52,349
FRODO:
<i>If you ask it of me...</i>

1692
02:43:52,724 --> 02:43:55,769
<i>...I will give you the One Ring.</i>

1693
02:43:56,853 --> 02:43:59,022
You offer it to me freely.

1694
02:44:03,610 --> 02:44:07,531
I do not deny that my heart
has greatly desired this.

1695
02:44:13,912 --> 02:44:17,207
In place of a Dark Lord,
you would have a queen...

1696
02:44:17,624 --> 02:44:21,461
...not dark but beautiful,
and terrible as the dawn!

1697
02:44:22,087 --> 02:44:25,132
Treacherous as the seal

1698
02:44:25,632 --> 02:44:30,554
Stronger than the foundations
of the earth!

1699
02:44:31,012 --> 02:44:33,390
All shall love me...

1700
02:44:33,598 --> 02:44:36,435
...and despair.

1701
02:44:50,532 --> 02:44:54,828
I pass the test. I will diminish...

1702
02:44:55,120 --> 02:44:57,581
...and go into the West...

1703
02:44:57,789 --> 02:45:02,252
-...and remain Galadriel.
- I cannot do this alone.

1704
02:45:05,839 --> 02:45:10,010
You are a Ring-bearer, Frodo.
To bear a Ring of Power...

1705
02:45:10,927 --> 02:45:12,429
...Is to be alone.

1706
02:45:15,765 --> 02:45:18,518
This is Nenya,
the Ring of Adamant.

1707
02:45:18,685 --> 02:45:20,312
And I am its keeper.

1708
02:45:23,523 --> 02:45:27,152
This task was appointed to you.

1709
02:45:28,195 --> 02:45:31,072
And if you do not find a way...

1710
02:45:32,282 --> 02:45:34,284
...no one will.

1711
02:45:34,659 --> 02:45:37,829
Then I know what I must do.

1712
02:45:38,497 --> 02:45:39,706
It's just...

1713
02:45:42,959 --> 02:45:45,212
...I'm afraid to do it.

1714
02:45:48,715 --> 02:45:53,845
Even the smallest person can change
the course of the future.

1715
02:45:59,184 --> 02:46:04,898
Do you know how the Orcs
first came into being?

1716
02:46:05,690 --> 02:46:09,027
They were Elves once.

1717
02:46:10,195 --> 02:46:13,532
Taken by the Dark Powers...

1718
02:46:13,740 --> 02:46:16,910
...tortured and mutilated.

1719
02:46:17,244 --> 02:46:22,541
A ruined and terrible form of life.

1720
02:46:22,832 --> 02:46:24,668
And now...

1721
02:46:26,127 --> 02:46:28,004
...perfected.

1722
02:46:28,713 --> 02:46:31,883
My fighting Uruk-hai...

1723
02:46:33,843 --> 02:46:36,179
...whom do you serve?

1724
02:46:36,388 --> 02:46:38,890
Saruman!

1725
02:46:59,744 --> 02:47:03,206
Hunt them down. Do not stop
until they are found.

1726
02:47:03,415 --> 02:47:06,293
You do not know pain.
You do not know fear.

1727
02:47:06,543 --> 02:47:09,462
You will taste Man-flesh!

1728
02:47:14,551 --> 02:47:18,263
One of the halflings carries
something of great value.

1729
02:47:18,430 --> 02:47:22,601
Bring them to me alive and unspoiled.

1730
02:47:24,436 --> 02:47:25,729
Kill the others.

1731
02:47:44,914 --> 02:47:50,337
CELEBORN: Never before have we clad
strangers in the garb of our own people.

1732
02:47:51,463 --> 02:47:55,300
May these cloaks help shield you
from unfriendly eyes.

1733
02:48:02,474 --> 02:48:04,017
Lembas.

1734
02:48:04,267 --> 02:48:05,852
Elvish waybread.

1735
02:48:08,355 --> 02:48:11,358
One small bite is enough to fill
the stomach of a grown man.

1736
02:48:17,864 --> 02:48:19,824
How many did you eat?

1737
02:48:19,991 --> 02:48:21,660
Four.

1738
02:48:23,161 --> 02:48:26,206
[BELCHES]

1739
02:48:27,457 --> 02:48:30,043
CELEBORN: <i> Every league you travel south,
the danger will increase.</i>

1740
02:48:30,251 --> 02:48:34,381
<i>Mordor Orcs now hold the eastern shore
of the Anduin.</i>

1741
02:48:34,547 --> 02:48:37,050
<i>Nor will you find safety
on the western bank.</i>

1742
02:48:37,258 --> 02:48:41,054
Strange creatures bearing the White Hand
have been seen on our borders.

1743
02:48:41,262 --> 02:48:46,351
Seldom do Orcs journey in the open
under the sun, yet these have done so.

1744
02:48:55,078 --> 02:48:57,697
[IN SINDARIN] <font color="#00bd00">(Le aphadar aen.)</font>

1745
02:48:59,030 --> 02:49:00,281
[IN WESTRON]
By river you have the chance...

1746
02:49:00,448 --> 02:49:03,660
...of outrunning the enemy
to the Falls of Rauros.

1747
02:49:20,927 --> 02:49:25,765
GALADRIEL: My gift for you, Legolas,
is a bow of the Galadhrim.

1748
02:49:26,015 --> 02:49:29,519
Worthy of the skill
of our woodland kin.

1749
02:49:34,899 --> 02:49:37,360
These are the daggers of the Noldorin.

1750
02:49:37,527 --> 02:49:41,531
They have already seen service in war.

1751
02:49:41,698 --> 02:49:43,950
Do not fear, young Peregrin Took.

1752
02:49:44,117 --> 02:49:47,454
<i>You will find your courage.</i>

1753
02:49:49,330 --> 02:49:51,291
<i>And for you, Samwise Gamgee...</i>

1754
02:49:51,458 --> 02:49:54,043
...Elven rope made of hithlain.

1755
02:49:54,210 --> 02:49:56,337
Thank you, my lady.

1756
02:49:58,118 --> 02:50:01,455
Have you run out
of those nice, shiny daggers?

1757
02:50:07,932 --> 02:50:10,977
And what gift would a dwarf ask
of the Elves?

1758
02:50:11,144 --> 02:50:13,271
Nothing.

1759
02:50:13,897 --> 02:50:17,233
Except to look upon the lady
of the Galadhrim one last time...

1760
02:50:17,859 --> 02:50:23,072
...for she is more fair
than all the jewels beneath the earth.

1761
02:50:30,121 --> 02:50:31,664
Actually...

1762
02:50:31,873 --> 02:50:33,500
There was one thing.

1763
02:50:34,334 --> 02:50:37,003
No, no, I'm talking nonsense.
It's quite impossible.

1764
02:50:37,170 --> 02:50:39,964
<i>Stupid to ask.</i>

1765
02:50:42,509 --> 02:50:44,636
GALADRIEL:
<i>I have nothing greater to give...</i>

1766
02:50:44,803 --> 02:50:48,389
...than the gift you already bear.

1767
02:50:49,613 --> 02:50:50,690
[IN SINDARIN] <font color="#00bd00">(Am meleth dîn,)</font>

1768
02:50:51,937 --> 02:50:57,305
<font color="#00bd00">(I ant e guil Arwen Undómiel pígatha.)</font>

1769
02:50:58,085 --> 02:51:01,411
[IN SINDARIN] <font color="#00bd00">(Aníron i e broniatha ad ae periatham,)</font>

1770
02:51:02,911 --> 02:51:05,873
<font color="#00bd00">(athar i methid en-amar hen.)</font>

1771
02:51:07,839 --> 02:51:13,591
<font color="#00bd00">(Aníron i e círatha na Valannor.)</font>

1772
02:51:14,040 --> 02:51:17,126
[IN WESTRON]
That choice is yet before her.

1773
02:51:17,710 --> 02:51:20,630
You have your own choice to make,
Aragorn.

1774
02:51:20,964 --> 02:51:26,803
To rise above the height of all
your fathers since the days of Elendil...

1775
02:51:26,970 --> 02:51:31,307
...or to fall into darkness
with all that is left of your kin.

1776
02:51:38,445 --> 02:51:39,783
[IN QUENYA] <font color="#0078bd">(Namárië.)</font>

1777
02:51:43,617 --> 02:51:47,034
[IN SINDARIN] <font color="#00bd00">(Nadath nâ i moe cerich.)</font>

1778
02:51:49,045 --> 02:51:50,133
But...
<font color="#00bd00">(Dan...)</font>

1779
02:51:53,507 --> 02:51:54,925
<font color="#00bd00">(Ú-'eveditham...)</font>

1780
02:51:54,949 --> 02:51:56,386
<font color="#00bd00">(Elessar.)</font>

1781
02:51:58,877 --> 02:52:02,088
[IN WESTRON]
<i>Farewell, Frodo Baggins.</i>

1782
02:52:02,255 --> 02:52:05,675
I give you the light of Eärendil...

1783
02:52:06,426 --> 02:52:08,761
...our most beloved star.

1784
02:52:17,896 --> 02:52:22,275
<i>May it be a light for you
in dark places...</i>

1785
02:52:22,525 --> 02:52:26,613
<i>...when all other lights go out.</i>

1786
02:52:35,455 --> 02:52:38,625
GIMLI: I have taken my worst wound
at this parting...

1787
02:52:39,250 --> 02:52:43,546
...having looked my last upon that
which is fairest.

1788
02:52:44,297 --> 02:52:47,634
Henceforth I will call nothing fair
unless it be her gift to me.

1789
02:52:47,884 --> 02:52:49,802
What was her gift?

1790
02:52:50,011 --> 02:52:54,933
I asked her for one hair
from her golden head.

1791
02:52:55,725 --> 02:52:58,603
She gave me three.

1792
02:54:04,127 --> 02:54:07,547
[BIRDS SQUAWKING]

1793
02:54:40,747 --> 02:54:44,208
Gollum. He has tracked us since Moria.

1794
02:54:47,920 --> 02:54:51,049
I had hoped we would lose him
on the river.

1795
02:54:51,257 --> 02:54:54,427
But he's too clever a waterman.

1796
02:54:55,261 --> 02:54:58,598
And if he alerts the enemy
to our whereabouts...

1797
02:54:58,765 --> 02:55:01,017
...it will make the crossing
even more dangerous.

1798
02:55:01,184 --> 02:55:03,269
SAM:
Have some food, Mr. Frodo.

1799
02:55:03,436 --> 02:55:06,522
-No, Sam.
-You haven't eaten anything all day.

1800
02:55:06,689 --> 02:55:09,776
You're not sleeping, neither.
Don't think I haven't noticed.

1801
02:55:10,735 --> 02:55:13,738
-Mr. Frodo--
-I'm all right.

1802
02:55:13,905 --> 02:55:15,073
But you're not.

1803
02:55:15,364 --> 02:55:17,867
I'm here to help you.

1804
02:55:18,034 --> 02:55:19,744
I promised Gandalf that I would.

1805
02:55:25,708 --> 02:55:28,461
You can't help me, Sam.

1806
02:55:30,588 --> 02:55:32,298
Not this time.

1807
02:55:35,218 --> 02:55:37,303
Get some sleep.

1808
02:55:43,559 --> 02:55:45,770
Minas Tirith is the safer road.

1809
02:55:46,312 --> 02:55:49,065
You know that.
From there we can regroup.

1810
02:55:49,732 --> 02:55:51,984
Strike out for Mordor from a place
of strength.

1811
02:55:52,318 --> 02:55:55,196
There is no strength in Gondor
that can avail us.

1812
02:55:55,655 --> 02:55:57,657
You were quick enough to trust
the Elves.

1813
02:55:59,492 --> 02:56:02,328
Have you so little faith
in your own people?

1814
02:56:02,495 --> 02:56:05,498
Yes, there is weakness.
There is frailty.

1815
02:56:05,706 --> 02:56:09,001
But there is courage also,
and honor to be found in Men.

1816
02:56:09,252 --> 02:56:11,462
But you will not see that.

1817
02:56:11,796 --> 02:56:13,214
You are afraid!

1818
02:56:13,464 --> 02:56:16,008
All your life, you have hidden
in the shadows.

1819
02:56:16,300 --> 02:56:19,762
Scared of who you are,
of what you are.

1820
02:56:22,181 --> 02:56:26,519
I will not lead the Ring within
a hundred leagues of your city.

1821
02:56:38,364 --> 02:56:39,740
Frodo.

1822
02:56:41,617 --> 02:56:43,119
The Argonath.

1823
02:56:43,759 --> 02:57:00,509
{\an8}[CHORUS SINGS IN QUENYA]:
<i>Out of the Great Sea to Middle-earth I am come.
<font color="#0078bd">(Et Eärello Endorenna utúlien.)</font></i>

1824
02:56:46,539 --> 02:56:50,293
Long have I desired
to look upon the kings of old.

1825
02:56:51,043 --> 02:56:52,962
My kin.

1826
02:57:00,521 --> 02:57:10,657
{\an8}<i>In this place will I abide,
<font color="#0078bd">(Sinomë maruvan ar Hildinyar,)</font></i>

1827
02:58:11,958 --> 02:58:14,126
We cross the lake at nightfall.

1828
02:58:14,377 --> 02:58:16,963
Hide the boats and continue on foot.

1829
02:58:17,129 --> 02:58:20,633
-We approach Mordor from the North.
-Oh, yes?

1830
02:58:21,050 --> 02:58:24,887
Just a simple matter of finding
our way through Emyn Muil...

1831
02:58:25,054 --> 02:58:28,307
...an impassable labyrinth
of razor-sharp rocks.

1832
02:58:28,474 --> 02:58:31,602
And after that, it gets even better.

1833
02:58:31,978 --> 02:58:36,941
Festering, stinking marshland
as far as the eye can see.

1834
02:58:37,108 --> 02:58:38,484
That is our road.

1835
02:58:40,069 --> 02:58:43,281
I suggest you take some rest
and recover your strength, Master Dwarf.

1836
02:58:43,489 --> 02:58:45,241
Recover my--

1837
02:58:48,244 --> 02:58:50,246
-We should leave now.
-No.

1838
02:58:50,413 --> 02:58:54,875
Orcs patrol the eastern shore.
We must wait for cover of darkness.

1839
02:58:55,084 --> 02:58:58,504
It is not the eastern shore
that worries me.

1840
02:58:58,754 --> 02:59:02,758
A shadow and a threat
has been growing in my mind.

1841
02:59:03,259 --> 02:59:07,430
Something draws near.
I can feel it.

1842
02:59:09,432 --> 02:59:14,395
Recover strength?
Pay no heed to that, young Hobbit.

1843
02:59:14,895 --> 02:59:16,605
Where's Frodo?

1844
02:59:42,214 --> 02:59:44,133
BOROMIR:
None of us should wander alone.

1845
02:59:45,551 --> 02:59:47,636
You, least of all.

1846
02:59:47,845 --> 02:59:50,306
So much depends on you.

1847
02:59:51,349 --> 02:59:53,309
Frodo?

1848
03:00:00,441 --> 03:00:02,985
I know why you seek solitude.

1849
03:00:03,694 --> 03:00:07,156
You suffer. I see it day by day.

1850
03:00:07,948 --> 03:00:10,993
You sure you do not suffer needlessly?

1851
03:00:12,578 --> 03:00:15,206
There are other ways, Frodo.

1852
03:00:15,456 --> 03:00:19,251
-Other paths that we might take.
-I know what you would say.

1853
03:00:19,502 --> 03:00:23,255
It would seem like wisdom
but for the warning in my heart.

1854
03:00:23,506 --> 03:00:26,592
Warning? Against what?

1855
03:00:26,759 --> 03:00:28,886
We're all afraid, Frodo.

1856
03:00:29,095 --> 03:00:32,723
But to let that fear drive us,
to destroy what hope we have...

1857
03:00:32,973 --> 03:00:36,727
-...don't you see that is madness?
-There is no other way.

1858
03:00:38,521 --> 03:00:41,857
I ask only for the strength
to defend my people!

1859
03:00:43,401 --> 03:00:45,486
-If you would but lend me the Ring.
-No.

1860
03:00:46,695 --> 03:00:50,366
-Why do you recoil? I am no thief.
-You are not yourself.

1861
03:00:52,201 --> 03:00:55,538
What chance do you think you have?

1862
03:00:55,704 --> 03:01:00,376
They will find you.
They will take the Ring.

1863
03:01:00,626 --> 03:01:04,296
And you will beg for death
before the end!

1864
03:01:05,469 --> 03:01:08,118
{\an8}THE RING [IN BLACK SPEECH]: <i> In the void...
<font color="#bd2600">(Gûm-ishi...)</font></i>

1865
03:01:06,643 --> 03:01:08,551
You fool!

1866
03:01:08,717 --> 03:01:12,409
It is not yours, save by unhappy chance!
It could have been mine.

1867
03:01:12,734 --> 03:01:13,709
It should be mine!
<i> </i>

1868
03:01:13,734 --> 03:01:14,987
{\an8}<i>...only...
<font color="#bd2600">(...ashi...)</font></i>

1869
03:01:14,312 --> 03:01:15,724
Give it to me!
<i> </i>

1870
03:01:15,891 --> 03:01:17,226
-Give it to me!
-No!

1871
03:01:17,250 --> 03:01:19,069
{\an8}<i>death.
<font color="#bd2600">(gurum.)</font></i>

1872
03:01:17,393 --> 03:01:19,228
-Give it to me!
-No.

1873
03:01:26,902 --> 03:01:28,904
I see your mind.

1874
03:01:29,155 --> 03:01:32,074
You will take the Ring to Sauron!

1875
03:01:32,283 --> 03:01:34,160
You will betray us!

1876
03:01:34,410 --> 03:01:37,580
You'll go to your death,
and the death of us all!

1877
03:01:38,038 --> 03:01:41,667
Curse you!
Curse you and all the halflings!

1878
03:01:48,757 --> 03:01:50,259
Frodo?

1879
03:01:54,597 --> 03:01:56,182
Frodo.

1880
03:02:00,102 --> 03:02:02,104
What have I done?

1881
03:02:02,313 --> 03:02:04,064
Please, Frodo.

1882
03:02:04,273 --> 03:02:06,942
Frodo, I'm sorry!

1883
03:02:07,151 --> 03:02:09,028
Frodo!

1884
03:02:34,486 --> 03:02:35,672
VOICE OF THE RING [IN BLACK SPEECH]: <i> Here...
<font color="#bd2600">(Akha...)</font></i>

1885
03:02:37,041 --> 03:02:41,028
<i>...only death.
<font color="#bd2600">(...ashi gurum.)</font></i>

1886
03:02:55,491 --> 03:02:56,909
Frodo?

1887
03:02:58,160 --> 03:03:01,247
-It has taken Boromir.
-Where is the Ring?

1888
03:03:01,497 --> 03:03:03,249
Stay away!

1889
03:03:03,666 --> 03:03:05,251
Frodo!

1890
03:03:07,503 --> 03:03:11,340
-I swore to protect you.
-Can you protect me from yourself?

1891
03:03:21,016 --> 03:03:23,519
Would you destroy it?

1892
03:03:28,524 --> 03:03:30,442
VOICE OF THE RING:
<i>Aragorn.</i>

1893
03:03:33,862 --> 03:03:36,198
<i>Aragorn.</i>

1894
03:03:38,033 --> 03:03:39,868
<i>Elessar.</i>

1895
03:03:47,543 --> 03:03:50,879
I would have gone with you to the end.

1896
03:03:51,547 --> 03:03:54,383
Into the very fires of Mordor.

1897
03:03:57,720 --> 03:03:58,887
I know.

1898
03:04:01,390 --> 03:04:06,812
Look after the others. Especially Sam.
He will not understand.

1899
03:04:10,566 --> 03:04:12,318
Go, Frodo!

1900
03:04:15,321 --> 03:04:16,822
Run.

1901
03:04:17,072 --> 03:04:18,741
Run!

1902
03:04:43,265 --> 03:04:44,933
Mr. Frodo!

1903
03:04:54,234 --> 03:04:55,986
Find the halfling!

1904
03:04:57,613 --> 03:05:00,157
Find the halfling!

1905
03:05:03,619 --> 03:05:05,287
Elendil!

1906
03:05:11,794 --> 03:05:13,379
Aragorn, go!

1907
03:05:35,067 --> 03:05:36,402
PIPPIN:
Frodo!

1908
03:05:36,985 --> 03:05:38,570
Hide here. Quick!

1909
03:05:39,196 --> 03:05:40,656
Come on!

1910
03:05:43,158 --> 03:05:45,160
What's he doing?

1911
03:05:49,415 --> 03:05:51,417
He's leaving.

1912
03:05:56,171 --> 03:05:59,091
-No!
-Pippin!

1913
03:06:04,012 --> 03:06:06,348
MERRY:
Run, Frodo. Go on!

1914
03:06:06,932 --> 03:06:10,018
-Hey! Hey, you!
-Over here!

1915
03:06:10,436 --> 03:06:12,020
-Over here!
-This way!

1916
03:06:22,865 --> 03:06:25,200
-It's working!
-I know it's working! Run!

1917
03:06:40,518 --> 03:06:56,468
{\an8}[CHORUS SINGS IN BLACK SPEECH]:
<i>One Ring for the Dark lord on his dark throne
<font color="#bd2600">(Ash Burz-Durbagu burzum-ishi)</font></i>

1918
03:07:18,670 --> 03:07:20,297
[HORN BLOWS]

1919
03:07:20,589 --> 03:07:23,634
-The horn of Gondor.
-Boromir.

1920
03:07:58,722 --> 03:08:16,422
{\an8}[CHORUS SINGS IN SINDARIN]:
<i>I do not love the bright sword for its sharpness
<font color="#00bd00">(Ú-velin i vegil an eigas)</font></i>

1921
03:08:06,718 --> 03:08:07,845
Run!

1922
03:08:16,580 --> 03:08:38,763
{\an8}<i>Nor the arrow for its swiftness
<font color="#00bd00">(Egor i bilin a lin[nas])</font></i>

1923
03:08:48,917 --> 03:08:59,080
{\an8}[CHORUS SINGS IN QUENYA]: <i> The tree is bare, the fountain still.
<font color="#0078bd">([I al]da helda, i ehtele lína.)</font></i>

1924
03:08:59,104 --> 03:09:18,104
{\an8}<i>Whither goest thou Boromir?
<font color="#0078bd">(Manna lelyalye Voromírë?)</font></i>

1925
03:09:18,128 --> 03:09:25,160
{\an8}<i>Your call...
<font color="#0078bd">(Cánalya...)</font></i>

1926
03:09:25,184 --> 03:09:30,481
{\an8}<i>Upon...
<font color="#0078bd">(Desse...)</font></i>

1927
03:09:30,505 --> 03:09:34,751
{\an8}<i>Now where?
<font color="#0078bd">(Sí massë?)</font></i>

1928
03:09:44,608 --> 03:09:47,027
[ARROW HITS]

1929
03:11:39,431 --> 03:11:41,058
No.

1930
03:11:44,895 --> 03:11:47,939
-They took the little ones.
-Hold still.

1931
03:11:48,273 --> 03:11:50,358
Frodo. Where is Frodo?

1932
03:11:52,235 --> 03:11:53,653
I let Frodo go.

1933
03:11:54,362 --> 03:11:56,948
Then you did what I could not.

1934
03:11:57,949 --> 03:12:01,286
I tried to take the Ring from him.

1935
03:12:01,787 --> 03:12:06,083
-The Ring is beyond our reach now.
-Forgive me.

1936
03:12:06,291 --> 03:12:08,585
I did not see it.

1937
03:12:08,794 --> 03:12:11,963
-I have failed you all.
-No, Boromir.

1938
03:12:12,422 --> 03:12:14,966
You fought bravely.

1939
03:12:15,258 --> 03:12:17,928
You have kept your honor.

1940
03:12:18,470 --> 03:12:20,430
BOROMIR:
Leave it.

1941
03:12:20,764 --> 03:12:22,808
It is over.

1942
03:12:23,975 --> 03:12:29,272
The world of Men will fall.
And all will come to darkness...

1943
03:12:29,689 --> 03:12:32,692
...and my city to ruin.

1944
03:12:36,780 --> 03:12:39,491
I do not know what strength
is in my blood...

1945
03:12:39,658 --> 03:12:43,662
...but I swear to you,
I will not let the White City fall...

1946
03:12:44,663 --> 03:12:47,165
...nor our people fail.

1947
03:12:48,166 --> 03:12:49,501
Our people.

1948
03:12:53,338 --> 03:12:55,465
Our people.

1949
03:13:17,195 --> 03:13:20,198
I would have followed you, my brother.

1950
03:13:21,741 --> 03:13:23,743
My captain.

1951
03:13:26,371 --> 03:13:28,331
My king.

1952
03:13:47,976 --> 03:13:50,228
Be at peace...

1953
03:13:50,562 --> 03:13:52,564
...son of Gondor.

1954
03:14:09,080 --> 03:14:12,417
They will look for his coming
from the White Tower.

1955
03:14:12,918 --> 03:14:15,921
But he will not return.

1956
03:14:39,110 --> 03:14:41,112
Frodo!

1957
03:15:00,590 --> 03:15:03,843
FRODO:
<i>I wish the Ring had never come to me.</i>

1958
03:15:05,136 --> 03:15:08,139
<i>I wish none of this had happened.</i>

1959
03:15:11,101 --> 03:15:13,853
GANDALF: <i> So do all who live
to see such times...</i>

1960
03:15:14,062 --> 03:15:17,482
<i>...but that is not for them to decide.</i>

1961
03:15:17,649 --> 03:15:20,318
<i>All you have to decide...</i>

1962
03:15:20,568 --> 03:15:25,323
...is what to do with the time
that is given to you.

1963
03:15:54,144 --> 03:15:56,187
Frodo, no!

1964
03:15:56,688 --> 03:15:58,023
Frodo!

1965
03:15:58,857 --> 03:16:01,526
-Mr. Frodo!
-No, Sam.

1966
03:16:05,030 --> 03:16:07,032
Go back, Sam!

1967
03:16:07,532 --> 03:16:11,119
-I'm going to Mordor alone.
-Of course you are.

1968
03:16:11,328 --> 03:16:14,164
And I'm coming with you!

1969
03:16:14,622 --> 03:16:17,042
You can't swim!

1970
03:16:20,837 --> 03:16:22,547
Sam!

1971
03:16:28,136 --> 03:16:29,429
Sam!

1972
03:17:10,387 --> 03:17:13,098
I made a promise, Mr. Frodo.

1973
03:17:13,431 --> 03:17:17,769
A promise:
"Don't you leave him, Samwise Gamgee."

1974
03:17:18,895 --> 03:17:21,481
And I don't mean to.

1975
03:17:21,773 --> 03:17:23,942
I don't mean to.

1976
03:17:25,610 --> 03:17:27,445
Sam.

1977
03:17:42,293 --> 03:17:43,962
Come on.

1978
03:18:12,449 --> 03:18:16,995
Hurry! Frodo and Sam
have reached the eastern shore.

1979
03:18:31,843 --> 03:18:36,848
-You mean not to follow them.
-Frodo's fate is no longer in our hands.

1980
03:18:40,310 --> 03:18:45,190
Then it has all been in vain.
The Fellowship has failed.

1981
03:18:57,035 --> 03:19:00,205
Not if we hold true to each other.

1982
03:19:01,539 --> 03:19:06,044
We will not abandon Merry and Pippin
to torment and death.

1983
03:19:07,045 --> 03:19:12,300
Not while we have strength left.
Leave all that can be spared behind.

1984
03:19:13,551 --> 03:19:15,595
We travel light.

1985
03:19:15,803 --> 03:19:17,722
Let us hunt some Orc.

1986
03:19:20,683 --> 03:19:22,727
Yes!

1987
03:19:41,704 --> 03:19:43,122
FRODO:
Mordor.

1988
03:19:43,748 --> 03:19:47,126
I hope the others find a safer road.

1989
03:19:48,086 --> 03:19:50,630
Strider will look after them.

1990
03:19:51,589 --> 03:19:54,926
I don't suppose
we'll ever see them again.

1991
03:19:55,260 --> 03:19:57,720
We may yet, Mr. Frodo.

1992
03:19:57,929 --> 03:19:59,430
We may.

1993
03:20:01,558 --> 03:20:02,600
Sam...

1994
03:20:06,229 --> 03:20:08,856
...I'm glad you are with me.

1995
03:21:08,322 --> 03:21:14,784
[ENYA IN WESTERON]: <i> May it be an evening star</i>

1996
03:21:14,808 --> 03:21:20,365
<i>Shines down upon you</i>

1997
03:21:21,968 --> 03:21:28,032
<i>May it be when darkness falls</i>

1998
03:21:28,056 --> 03:21:34,625
<i>Your heart will be true</i>

1999
03:21:35,212 --> 03:21:41,387
<i>You walk a lonely road</i>

2000
03:21:41,411 --> 03:21:50,922
<i>Oh! How far you are from home</i>

2001
03:21:52,002 --> 03:22:03,585
[ENYA IN QUENYA]: <i> Darkness has come
<font color="#0078bd">(Mornie utúlië)</font></i>

2002
03:22:03,609 --> 03:22:15,526
[IN WESTRON] <i>Believe and you will find your way</i>

2003
03:22:15,550 --> 03:22:27,968
[IN QUENYA] <i>Darkness has fallen
<font color="#0078bd">(Mornie alantië)</font></i>

2004
03:22:27,992 --> 03:22:39,402
[IN WESTRON] <i>A promise lives within you now</i>

2005
03:22:42,558 --> 03:22:48,609
<i>May it be the shadow's call</i>

2006
03:22:48,633 --> 03:22:54,086
<i>Will fly away</i>

2007
03:22:55,632 --> 03:23:01,537
<i>May it be you journey on</i>

2008
03:23:01,561 --> 03:23:06,927
<i>To light the day</i>

2009
03:23:08,066 --> 03:23:14,415
<i>When the night is overcome</i>

2010
03:23:14,439 --> 03:23:23,212
<i>You may rise to find the sun</i>

2011
03:23:24,483 --> 03:23:36,149
[IN QUENYA] <i>Darkness has come
<font color="#0078bd">(Mornie utúlië)</font></i>

2012
03:23:36,173 --> 03:23:47,753
[IN WESTRON] <i>Believe and you will find your way</i>

2013
03:23:47,778 --> 03:23:59,532
[IN QUENYA] <i>Darkness has fallen
<font color="#0078bd">(Mornie alantië)</font></i>

2014
03:23:59,556 --> 03:24:11,965
[IN WESTRON] <i>A promise lives within you now</i>

2015
03:24:11,991 --> 03:24:24,076
<i>A promise lives within you...</i>

2016
03:24:24,100 --> 03:24:31,400
<i>...now</i>

2017
03:25:08,430 --> 03:25:14,835
<i>When the cold of winter comes</i>

2018
03:25:14,859 --> 03:25:21,206
<i>Starless night will cover day</i>

2019
03:25:21,230 --> 03:25:27,396
<i>In the veiling of the sun</i>

2020
03:25:27,420 --> 03:25:34,353
<i>We will walk in bitter rain</i>

2021
03:25:34,640 --> 03:25:39,676
<i>But in dreams</i>

2022
03:25:39,700 --> 03:25:46,670
<i>I can hear your name</i>

2023
03:25:46,694 --> 03:25:52,592
<i>And in dreams</i>

2024
03:25:52,616 --> 03:26:03,703
<i>We will meet again</i>

2025
03:26:22,376 --> 03:26:28,229
<i>When the seas and mountains fall</i>

2026
03:26:28,254 --> 03:26:34,946
<i>And we come, to end of days</i>

2027
03:26:34,970 --> 03:26:41,244
<i>In the dark I hear a call</i>

2028
03:26:41,268 --> 03:26:44,344
<i>Calling me there</i>

2029
03:26:44,765 --> 03:26:47,931
<i>I will go there</i>

2030
03:26:47,955 --> 03:26:53,115
<i>And back again.</i>

2031
03:26:53,139 --> 03:27:13,339
[CHORUS IN SINDARIN]: <i> Here Elbereth Star-kindler,
<font color="#00bd00">(Nef Elbereth Gilthoniel,)</font></i>

2032
03:27:13,363 --> 03:27:35,025
<i>Glittering slants down like sparkling jewels
<font color="#00bd00">(Silivren penna míriel)</font></i>

